  6c112a85-0d61-4728-8690-e20820b2da39:
    id: 6c112a85-0d61-4728-8690-e20820b2da39
    content: The idea of blueprints is that you can share and refine them with your team, or open source them to share with a community. If you have blueprints you would like to share, you can make a merge request to add them to the project defaults.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
      resolvedAt: '2026-02-18T09:21:21.550Z'
  72c076b7-f7c6-4972-9c00-34eaab2dde1d:
    id: 72c076b7-f7c6-4972-9c00-34eaab2dde1d
    content: All arbo files including blueprints are in YAML format and human readable, so you can commit arbo files to your git projects and review the changes with your colleauges.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      resolvedAt: '2026-02-18T09:21:21.550Z'
