  cba911e8-bdc3-43ed-b39b-51f50165e224:
    id: cba911e8-bdc3-43ed-b39b-51f50165e224
    content: 'Step 1 (S): Extend `TransientMetadata` with `executionState` field in `src/shared/types/treeNode.ts`'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: abandoned
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  9f0930b5-1b36-42b2-96b3-e6da98e0ff4b:
    id: 9f0930b5-1b36-42b2-96b3-e6da98e0ff4b
    content: 'Step 2 (M): Create `executionStore.ts` — standalone Zustand store tracking `Record<nodeId, { terminalId, state }>` for all active executions, plus actions: `startExecution`, `pauseExecution`, `resumeExecution`, `releaseTerminal`, `recoverOnRestart`'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: abandoned
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  a5818e2a-eb21-4e31-83b2-6d69068f6d5a:
    id: a5818e2a-eb21-4e31-83b2-6d69068f6d5a
    content: 'Step 3 (M): Create execution eligibility helper in `src/renderer/utils/workflowHelpers.ts` — `isEligibleForExecution(nodeId, nodes, ancestorRegistry)`: node is direct child of a workflow step or workflow root, is not itself a step/workflow/context, and is not already running'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  8d9a3708-13a9-4237-8d4b-8b66b1576f64:
    id: 8d9a3708-13a9-4237-8d4b-8b66b1576f64
    content: 'Step 4 (M): Create `useWorkflowExecutionSubmenu.ts` hook — builds "Start Workflow" / "Pause Workflow" / "Resume Workflow" menu items; "Start" checks terminal availability and shows toast if unavailable; Pause/Resume positioned as first menu option'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  3dfce498-870c-469b-8626-577271f4d805:
    id: 3dfce498-870c-469b-8626-577271f4d805
    content: 'Step 5 (S): Integrate execution submenu into `useNodeContextMenu.ts` — call new submenu builder, insert execution items before existing items'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  d867db58-03ca-4f3c-88a2-84abe2775678:
    id: d867db58-03ca-4f3c-88a2-84abe2775678
    content: 'Step 6 (M): Create `useWorkflowExecutionOverlay.ts` hook — returns overlay component props (icon, onClick handler, visibility) based on node''s execution state; overlay renders Play icon for Running, Pause icon for Paused, nothing for Idle'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  47fd2988-8fa2-4735-93fa-1f9ee27119c3:
    id: 47fd2988-8fa2-4735-93fa-1f9ee27119c3
    content: 'Step 7 (M): Add overlay rendering in `NodeContent.tsx` — new `<span>` with click handler positioned to avoid conflict with existing workflow indicator (`left: -10px`) and step number; execution overlay positioned on the right side of the icon wrapper or as a badge'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  14cbd16a-950a-4796-8477-86400b6c1191:
    id: 14cbd16a-950a-4796-8477-86400b6c1191
    content: 'Step 8 (S): Add CSS for execution overlays in `NodeContent.css` — positioned at `right: -12px` to avoid left-side conflict; play icon with green tint, pause icon with amber tint; clickable with `pointer-events: auto` and `cursor: pointer`'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  7e54e9a4-0a13-45a6-af10-8688cce4296d:
    id: 7e54e9a4-0a13-45a6-af10-8688cce4296d
    content: 'Step 9 (M): Add node-move-on-start logic — when starting a node at the workflow root, use existing `dropNode` action to move it to first step''s children; determine first step via `findNextStepTarget` from workflow helpers'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  6c8d8ed5-8a27-488e-9deb-0b92810c4329:
    id: 6c8d8ed5-8a27-488e-9deb-0b92810c4329
    content: 'Step 10 (S): Add Escape key handler in `editingService.ts` — after cancel-edit check fails (node not being edited), check if active node is Running and call `pauseExecution`; only fires when not in edit mode'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  c5e46e64-5223-49a2-b4f6-fc8c6e6317dc:
    id: c5e46e64-5223-49a2-b4f6-fc8c6e6317dc
    content: 'Step 11 (S): Add startup recovery — in app initialization (or store hydration), scan all nodes for `transient.executionState === ''running''`, set them to `''paused''`, show single aggregate toast'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
