  c98f152a-667e-4a98-9c0f-f2cf85ee7875:
    id: c98f152a-667e-4a98-9c0f-f2cf85ee7875
    content: Arborescent is an outliner for project decomposition and AI workflows. It prioritizes focus, low cognitive load, predictable behavior, and emergent complexity. The tree structure supports non-linear thinking while minimizing visual noise. The goal is full creative and technical control over AI interactions through reusable contexts and shareable blueprints.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
      isBlueprint: false
  834f8cb8-fe9d-40e7-8b07-cd05231bf425:
    id: 834f8cb8-fe9d-40e7-8b07-cd05231bf425
    content: 'Current relevant features: tree-based decomposition, contexts (collaborate/execute modes), blueprints, workflows with step types (manual/checkpoint/autonomous), feedback panel for collaborate mode, hook system for AI tool integration.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
      isBlueprint: false
  cfe7db63-13ec-4716-adb9-1d0746bd24f6:
    id: cfe7db63-13ec-4716-adb9-1d0746bd24f6
    content: Review the project philosophy and existing feature set
    children:
      - c98f152a-667e-4a98-9c0f-f2cf85ee7875
      - 834f8cb8-fe9d-40e7-8b07-cd05231bf425
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
      isBlueprint: false
  40ac0971-a82b-4056-bce3-6c64cde2c8d0:
    id: 40ac0971-a82b-4056-bce3-6c64cde2c8d0
    content: The target user builds structured projects with AI assistance — developers, architects, team leads who want AI to handle decomposition and execution while they maintain creative control.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
      isBlueprint: false
  b54cc66a-55d0-405d-a638-e43a70d19fbc:
    id: b54cc66a-55d0-405d-a638-e43a70d19fbc
    content: 'Pain point 1: The feedback panel requires manual acceptance for every AI response, creating friction in multi-step decomposition workflows (problem statement → user stories → specs → tests → code).'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
      isBlueprint: false
  e52ece9b-5928-4654-955f-b232c0409e68:
    id: e52ece9b-5928-4654-955f-b232c0409e68
    content: 'Pain point 2: Accepting feedback replaces the original subtree — no way to keep the source material alongside the AI output, losing the audit trail of how a problem statement evolved.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
      isBlueprint: false
  c0e3eb26-d333-4859-ae52-56672df1a439:
    id: c0e3eb26-d333-4859-ae52-56672df1a439
    content: 'Pain point 3: Tree bloat from accumulated contexts, specifications, and decomposition artifacts with no way to manage scale.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
      isBlueprint: false
  bc8c1b0f-af17-4a38-a5c5-3fc29d78990d:
    id: bc8c1b0f-af17-4a38-a5c5-3fc29d78990d
    content: 'Pain point 4: Workflow step configuration is getting complex — right-click context menus aren''t sufficient for managing output modes, step types, and other per-step settings.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
      isBlueprint: false
  545f1dc2-65cb-4510-9101-b60beb43c465:
    id: 545f1dc2-65cb-4510-9101-b60beb43c465
