  e02bcf04-3001-4f2b-9ab6-c24d17de5176:
    id: e02bcf04-3001-4f2b-9ab6-c24d17de5176
    content: The command pattern (AcceptFeedbackCommand) currently treats feedback as an atomic subtree replacement — the collaborating node's ID is preserved but all descendants get fresh UUIDs. Any new approach must remain undoable.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
      isBlueprint: false
  3483691b-fb4a-4176-9898-bcbf452224cc:
    id: 3483691b-fb4a-4176-9898-bcbf452224cc
    content: Contexts and blueprints are tightly coupled to tree position — creating new nodes must preserve applied context inheritance and blueprint membership.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
      isBlueprint: false
  33e4fc54-80ed-4857-9906-8306a05f1c56:
    id: 33e4fc54-80ed-4857-9906-8306a05f1c56
    content: The current YAML-based .arbo file format stores the entire tree in a single file. This is simple but doesn't scale to very large trees.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
      isBlueprint: false
  f8a02f07-c2b3-4a9e-891c-2413cf7955e7:
    id: f8a02f07-c2b3-4a9e-891c-2413cf7955e7
    content: Workflow automation relies on hook events from external AI tools — the system is already designed for async, event-driven progression.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
      isBlueprint: false
