      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
      isBlueprint: false
  1b1634f8-abc0-485d-9e74-61ed39ff8f2e:
    id: 1b1634f8-abc0-485d-9e74-61ed39ff8f2e
    content: Every user who builds multi-step AI workflows hits this wall. It's the difference between Arborescent being a prompt manager and being a true workflow orchestrator. This is the core use case — it affects power users on every project.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
      isBlueprint: false
  bb2e4650-7051-43d8-9d2e-389c664c6bde:
    id: bb2e4650-7051-43d8-9d2e-389c664c6bde
    content: Assess who is affected and how frequently
    children:
      - 1b1634f8-abc0-485d-9e74-61ed39ff8f2e
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
      isBlueprint: false
  fc94ebe4-9c76-4b59-88a6-69e9d7902203:
    id: fc94ebe4-9c76-4b59-88a6-69e9d7902203
    content: 'Today: User writes a problem statement → sends with collaborate context → waits → reads feedback → clicks Accept (original is gone) → applies next context → sends again → waits → clicks Accept → repeat. For a 5-step decomposition with 10 user stories, that''s 50+ manual interventions. Users either give up on deep decomposition or do it outside Arborescent.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
      isBlueprint: false
  3e289922-2f73-4797-9566-c0727f590909:
    id: 3e289922-2f73-4797-9566-c0727f590909
    content: Identify what happens today without a solution
    children:
      - fc94ebe4-9c76-4b59-88a6-69e9d7902203
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
      isBlueprint: false
  77534829-9497-4510-8e28-b3b77c440c72:
    id: 77534829-9497-4510-8e28-b3b77c440c72
    content: Yes. The deeper issue is that the feedback panel was designed for single-node collaboration, not for pipeline-style transformation. The system treats AI output as a replacement, not as an addition. The workflow system can move items through steps, but it can't create new tree structure from AI output and feed it forward. These are two halves of the same orchestration problem.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
      isBlueprint: false
  1cc091c2-e715-441f-a94e-4c0af44cd370:
    id: 1cc091c2-e715-441f-a94e-4c0af44cd370
    content: Flag if the problem is symptoms of a deeper issue
    children:
      - 77534829-9497-4510-8e28-b3b77c440c72
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
      isBlueprint: false
  c67f27e5-55a7-486e-81b5-a65f818bdc12:
    id: c67f27e5-55a7-486e-81b5-a65f818bdc12
    content: Analyze the problem or opportunity
    children:
      - bd4bee12-f9e2-45c0-84fa-b610df86cf89
      - bb2e4650-7051-43d8-9d2e-389c664c6bde
      - 3e289922-2f73-4797-9566-c0727f590909
      - 1cc091c2-e715-441f-a94e-4c0af44cd370
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
