  d4c54a1e-7851-4413-a513-5f27eaaa3751:
    id: d4c54a1e-7851-4413-a513-5f27eaaa3751
    content: 'Highest likelihood of defects: AcceptFeedbackCommand multi-root undo — must correctly snapshot parent''s children array, remove all created subtrees, and restore the original node in the correct position. More moving parts than single-root undo.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  b039a361-fdd0-4067-a711-b49324e8f997:
    id: b039a361-fdd0-4067-a711-b49324e8f997
    content: 'Highest impact if failed: backward compatibility — if the decomposition flag is not correctly checked, existing single-root acceptance could break for all users. Every modified function must branch on the flag before changing behavior.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  db82f5e8-6465-4f56-92e0-84c53d7aefe9:
    id: db82f5e8-6465-4f56-92e0-84c53d7aefe9
    content: 'Dependency: the decomposition flag must be threaded through the collaborate flow (collaborateActions → processIncomingFeedbackContent → extractFeedbackContent → AcceptFeedbackCommand). A break in any link silently falls back to single-root mode, which is safe but confusing if the user expects multi-root.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  2a37b438-28f1-4d39-9b15-90aee2a33649:
    id: 2a37b438-28f1-4d39-9b15-90aee2a33649
    content: 'Ambiguity: the AC says "Created nodes inherit the applied context and blueprint membership of their position in the tree, unless overridden by inherited metadata from the parent." The override precedence needs clarification during implementation — does parent metadata win over position-based inheritance, or vice versa?'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  1ad7004e-2afe-4591-818b-62a3ded47a1e:
