  2ec744ef-ac36-40bf-9b6a-fdf99391131f:
    id: 2ec744ef-ac36-40bf-9b6a-fdf99391131f
    content: Review the project philosophy and existing feature set
    children:
      - 28d9379b-fc9f-4587-854a-2adf1fdcb2c6
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  28d9379b-fc9f-4587-854a-2adf1fdcb2c6:
    id: 28d9379b-fc9f-4587-854a-2adf1fdcb2c6
    content: Arborescent's workflow automation runs items through sequential steps with human validation checkpoints. Currently, the AI has no way to signal back to Arborescent that it needs the user's attention — it can only complete normally (Stop hook) or fail silently. If the AI discovers a problem mid-execution (spec issues, ambiguity, technical constraints), the workflow continues blindly or the user only notices when reviewing output later.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  bbdc5b52-a9eb-42a5-bdd4-86ef7ede2d8f:
    id: bbdc5b52-a9eb-42a5-bdd4-86ef7ede2d8f
    content: Identify the target user and their current pain points
    children:
      - 114f27d5-6105-44ea-8922-fb0d3827bd97
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  114f27d5-6105-44ea-8922-fb0d3827bd97:
    id: 114f27d5-6105-44ea-8922-fb0d3827bd97
    content: Users running autonomous workflow chains where the AI encounters issues that require human judgement. The AI finishes its task but the output is compromised because it couldn't flag the problem in real time. The user discovers this only when reviewing the final result, wasting the work done in subsequent automated steps.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  a870d2f7-69f2-4c36-bb0c-cc122d09db0c:
    id: a870d2f7-69f2-4c36-bb0c-cc122d09db0c
    content: Note any technical or design constraints worth respecting
    children:
      - c644cbb3-7aec-466a-a1a1-c32e889966d1
      - 9ad43074-d715-4750-b67e-a877d92ee45e
      - 2fc4343d-ada2-48e4-9771-abeeb4ad01d6
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  c644cbb3-7aec-466a-a1a1-c32e889966d1:
    id: c644cbb3-7aec-466a-a1a1-c32e889966d1
    content: The hook infrastructure already exists — Arborescent runs a local HTTP server that receives hook events with session_id, hook_event_name, and an optional message field. Adding a new hook_event_name is straightforward.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  9ad43074-d715-4750-b67e-a877d92ee45e:
    id: 9ad43074-d715-4750-b67e-a877d92ee45e
    content: Claude Code hooks support custom commands, so the AI can be instructed to call a curl endpoint when it needs to flag an issue.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  2fc4343d-ada2-48e4-9771-abeeb4ad01d6:
    id: 2fc4343d-ada2-48e4-9771-abeeb4ad01d6
    content: The AI would need to be told about this capability via the context instructions — it can't discover it on its own.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  dd75fcfe-7066-49a0-be26-29697c853fa5:
    id: dd75fcfe-7066-49a0-be26-29697c853fa5
    content: Analyze the problem or opportunity
    children:
      - 228cc374-870b-4627-9a0d-40ef1ffd713f
      - c7aa1ea6-95fc-4f38-9e91-48b92ccd032d
      - bf14c42f-0b8a-41dd-929c-baa33bc93392
      - 3ef57efd-1903-4b4d-a900-8b8583fe5f8d
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  228cc374-870b-4627-9a0d-40ef1ffd713f:
    id: 228cc374-870b-4627-9a0d-40ef1ffd713f
    content: Restate the problem in the user's language
    children:
      - aaaf92e8-8596-4479-b4bc-854613d67e82
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  aaaf92e8-8596-4479-b4bc-854613d67e82:
    id: aaaf92e8-8596-4479-b4bc-854613d67e82
    content: '"When the AI hits a problem during an automated workflow, it just carries on. I want it to be able to raise its hand and say ''I need your input'' — and for the workflow to pause until I deal with it."'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  c7aa1ea6-95fc-4f38-9e91-48b92ccd032d:
    id: c7aa1ea6-95fc-4f38-9e91-48b92ccd032d
    content: Assess who is affected and how frequently
    children:
      - 167d076b-2589-4600-8388-124fc1be0548
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  167d076b-2589-4600-8388-124fc1be0548:
    id: 167d076b-2589-4600-8388-124fc1be0548
    content: Every user running autonomous workflows. The frequency depends on task complexity — simple generation tasks rarely need intervention, but decomposition, spec writing, and code generation frequently encounter ambiguities or constraints.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  bf14c42f-0b8a-41dd-929c-baa33bc93392:
    id: bf14c42f-0b8a-41dd-929c-baa33bc93392
    content: Identify what happens today without a solution
    children:
