  9ec63e5f-3c83-413b-ab51-138298c5c33c:
    id: 9ec63e5f-3c83-413b-ab51-138298c5c33c
    content: The destination picker UX is the biggest design risk — pasting a hyperlink is functional but not discoverable. A tree browser/dropdown would be better UX but significantly more effort.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  da4b29e9-1178-448f-ae8a-627e7cfa8833:
    id: da4b29e9-1178-448f-ae8a-627e7cfa8833
    content: 'The archive operation adds complexity to AcceptFeedbackCommand which is already the most complex command. The undo path must correctly restore: original node position, archive destination children order, all created relation nodes, and the replacement nodes.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  83b88404-810b-4eb2-a3b3-6c47f7b30d6d:
    id: 83b88404-810b-4eb2-a3b3-6c47f7b30d6d
    content: If the user runs the same item through the same workflow step multiple times (e.g., after undo), the archive destination accumulates duplicate copies. This is by design but could be confusing.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  68e4f3b0-08ad-4530-8d09-803eeb02d3bf:
    id: 68e4f3b0-08ad-4530-8d09-803eeb02d3bf
    content: '"Resolve linked content when sending" interacts with the existing hyperlink resolution in exportContextAsMarkdown. If the replacement node is inside a context declaration, its hyperlinks already resolve. The flag may need to force resolution even outside context declarations — this needs investigation.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  55041df7-1f4e-4a70-a755-4ca6953faae2:
    id: 55041df7-1f4e-4a70-a755-4ca6953faae2
    content: Blueprint export includes relation link nodes as-is, which may create broken hyperlinks in the exported blueprint (the linked nodes won't exist in the new file). This is an edge case noted as acceptable.
