  e627b175-f677-464c-9eff-48a46d051552:
    id: e627b175-f677-464c-9eff-48a46d051552
    content: Risks
    children:
      - 74ab6c85-2b27-4f11-8f80-a4590d9424e0
      - 6da67bde-aad6-4f36-83d3-f6cdce9f9d7d
      - 18e4dce9-c7eb-41d5-a0cd-11c68bfa29c0
      - 47f00c92-80a1-42ce-9aab-3141b73e2952
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  74ab6c85-2b27-4f11-8f80-a4590d9424e0:
    id: 74ab6c85-2b27-4f11-8f80-a4590d9424e0
    content: 'Highest likelihood of defects: timing between current node completion and next node startup. If the terminal is still assigned to the previous node, the startWorkflow guard rejects the next one. The delay must be sufficient for cleanup.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  6da67bde-aad6-4f36-83d3-f6cdce9f9d7d:
    id: 6da67bde-aad6-4f36-83d3-f6cdce9f9d7d
    content: 'Highest impact if failed: infinite recursion without the safety limit. A workflow that creates output feeding back into itself would loop forever, consuming terminal resources and creating unlimited nodes.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  18e4dce9-c7eb-41d5-a0cd-11c68bfa29c0:
    id: 18e4dce9-c7eb-41d5-a0cd-11c68bfa29c0
    content: 'Dependency: recurse relies on the terminal being available after the previous node completes. The completeWorkflow function clears the execution state, which frees the terminal — but there may be a race condition if the recurse check runs before setState propagates.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  47f00c92-80a1-42ce-9aab-3141b73e2952:
    id: 47f00c92-80a1-42ce-9aab-3141b73e2952
    content: 'Ambiguity: the spec says "walks back through autonomous steps" — this means walking backwards through the workflow''s children array from the current step, checking stepType metadata. The boundary condition (what counts as "first" when the workflow starts with the autonomous chain) needs to be precise.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  e27ceff0-92dc-4f4a-b5df-5a6388ff6431:
    id: e27ceff0-92dc-4f4a-b5df-5a6388ff6431
    content: Problem statement
    children:
      - 3c08691d-c3b7-4d95-91f4-d94e07b8396c
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  3c08691d-c3b7-4d95-91f4-d94e07b8396c:
    id: 3c08691d-c3b7-4d95-91f4-d94e07b8396c
    content: As a user running an autonomous workflow step with a collaborate-mode context, the AI finishes and writes feedback, but nothing happens automatically — I must manually accept the feedback before the workflow can continue
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  1d57738d-bd30-4a28-9d50-13f4a0c333d0:
    id: 1d57738d-bd30-4a28-9d50-13f4a0c333d0
    content: Use cases
    children:
