  438ff371-9aa3-40eb-99b2-f101fe3e88ae:
    id: 438ff371-9aa3-40eb-99b2-f101fe3e88ae
    content: The single collaboratingNodeId constraint only applies to manual/checkpoint collaborations (panel is a singleton). Autonomous collaborations need a separate tracking mechanism keyed by node or terminal, since they don't use the panel.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  259a113a-a4e0-4c46-839c-6f06c36d0f9e:
    id: 259a113a-a4e0-4c46-839c-6f06c36d0f9e
    content: The singleton FeedbackFileWatcher and the assumption that all feedback content belongs to one collaboratingNodeId are the two main architectural barriers to concurrent autonomous collaborations. Both need to be addressed.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  d2f4ad82-f086-4365-9e0d-5843d9e8c113:
    id: d2f4ad82-f086-4365-9e0d-5843d9e8c113
    content: processIncomingFeedbackContent currently has no validation that incoming content was intended for the active node — for concurrent autonomous collaborations, the file watcher callback must include the node ID so content is routed to the correct collaboration
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
