  071563c9-a7cb-415d-9da6-7b539668cba3:
    id: 071563c9-a7cb-415d-9da6-7b539668cba3
    content: Refactor keyboard listeners
    children:
      - 7efbfd95-39a8-40ab-8e74-8ba61ceb999d
      - 77070583-125f-4d51-9b56-1b900c1c6a05
      - f9c25e60-cc2d-4e4d-8d4c-b9a91bcca87d
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: false
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  7efbfd95-39a8-40ab-8e74-8ba61ceb999d:
    id: 7efbfd95-39a8-40ab-8e74-8ba61ceb999d
    content: 'US1: Register keyboard listeners on window and remove DOM element ref dependency'
    children:
      - c7fbd549-738a-4e47-a6da-596a3fb32fc9
      - d288aea9-9ee4-4d8e-b04e-f6b48bc2c3f5
      - 8705cf75-b22e-44f8-97ca-fb4296e04695
      - e9f30def-b9ef-4767-9bd8-10a5ba63fa85
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  c7fbd549-738a-4e47-a6da-596a3fb32fc9:
    id: c7fbd549-738a-4e47-a6da-596a3fb32fc9
    content: Problem statement
    children:
      - 6f997326-ecde-441a-a771-3dc13e8d60a9
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  6f997326-ecde-441a-a771-3dc13e8d60a9:
    id: 6f997326-ecde-441a-a771-3dc13e8d60a9
    content: As a user, keyboard shortcuts intermittently fail on app startup, requiring a reload (Ctrl+R) to fix. This happens because keyboard listeners are registered on a DOM element ref that may not exist when the registration effect first runs, and React doesn't re-trigger the effect when the ref's .current changes. The current architecture registers listeners on container DOM elements and maintains a registry to map elements to stores, but every handler ignores the registration target and finds the active store via document.activeElement. The element-scoped registration adds complexity (refs, registry, HMR workaround) without providing any functional benefit.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  d288aea9-9ee4-4d8e-b04e-f6b48bc2c3f5:
    id: d288aea9-9ee4-4d8e-b04e-f6b48bc2c3f5
    content: Use cases
    children:
      - 7e2c33cd-3197-4634-81a1-262cf3fe0577
      - 1e121bcc-fa69-4c5a-9f0c-bebc4af70029
      - c1cf012b-ae29-49c5-a6c1-f237918a7f27
      - 63a66e0f-bd02-4411-8b42-bdde196a79bc
      - e51c7f34-e0e3-4070-90af-66b6eac0f456
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  7e2c33cd-3197-4634-81a1-262cf3fe0577:
    id: 7e2c33cd-3197-4634-81a1-262cf3fe0577
    content: 'Primary: User launches the app for the first time. Keyboard shortcuts work immediately without needing to reload.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  1e121bcc-fa69-4c5a-9f0c-bebc4af70029:
    id: 1e121bcc-fa69-4c5a-9f0c-bebc4af70029
    content: 'Secondary: User opens multiple files in tabs and switches between them. Keyboard shortcuts always operate on the correct tree — the one that has focus.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  c1cf012b-ae29-49c5-a6c1-f237918a7f27:
    id: c1cf012b-ae29-49c5-a6c1-f237918a7f27
    content: 'Secondary: User opens the feedback panel and uses keyboard navigation within the feedback tree. Navigation and editing shortcuts work in the feedback tree. UI shortcuts (cut/copy/paste/undo/redo at app level) only fire when focus is in the main workspace tree, not the feedback tree.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: abandoned
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
