  d56fad58-145b-4eb0-984a-a31cdb2978c2:
    id: d56fad58-145b-4eb0-984a-a31cdb2978c2
    content: Risks
    children:
      - f9b22b14-c787-4404-9f2d-febd6f830064
      - 821c1676-7e79-45b8-8005-0e13a1aa75ad
      - 627eca9f-ee97-40f7-bf1d-4dc8e01d3d01
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  f9b22b14-c787-4404-9f2d-febd6f830064:
    id: f9b22b14-c787-4404-9f2d-febd6f830064
    content: 'Highest likelihood of defects: the store lookup change. If getActiveStore returns the wrong store or null in a case where the old registry returned the correct one, shortcuts will silently fail or operate on the wrong tree. The old system had a lastActiveStore fallback that the new system replaces with the active file''s store — verify these behave equivalently.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  821c1676-7e79-45b8-8005-0e13a1aa75ad:
    id: 821c1676-7e79-45b8-8005-0e13a1aa75ad
    content: 'Highest impact if failed: all keyboard shortcuts broken. This is a structural change to the keyboard system — if the listener registration doesn''t fire, nothing works. The manual first-launch test is the critical validation.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  627eca9f-ee97-40f7-bf1d-4dc8e01d3d01:
    id: 627eca9f-ee97-40f7-bf1d-4dc8e01d3d01
    content: The feedback panel guard relies on DOM class name (.feedback-panel). If the class name changes or the feedback panel DOM structure changes, UI shortcuts could leak into the feedback panel. This is fragile but no more so than the previous element-scoped approach.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
