      plugins: {}
  a04aabb2-4d9c-4ea4-960e-081b87114040:
    id: a04aabb2-4d9c-4ea4-960e-081b87114040
    content: 'Highest likelihood of defects: the built-in defaults logic. The conditional display (hidden when inherited) and the special handling of "Basic execution" via BASIC_EXECUTE_CONTEXT_ID are the most complex parts.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  bbd8d32f-bc9d-459d-bcb5-c0c9292d5785:
    id: bbd8d32f-bc9d-459d-bcb5-c0c9292d5785
    content: 'Highest impact if failed: applying the wrong context or mode. If "Basic execution" incorrectly sets the context to null instead of BASIC_EXECUTE_CONTEXT_ID, the node would use collaborate mode when the user expects execute mode.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  8d5fe45d-4712-4617-b2a7-78d99c5d441c:
    id: 8d5fe45d-4712-4617-b2a7-78d99c5d441c
    content: The CSS scrolling change is global. If it causes visual issues in other submenus (unexpected scrollbars, clipped content), it needs to be scoped specifically to submenus with the context picker.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  3a84a223-538b-417b-a265-8e128c1edfc0:
