  7f69689b-2d9e-4ac2-9ba0-8346f49b6344:
    id: 7f69689b-2d9e-4ac2-9ba0-8346f49b6344
    content: The collaborate pipeline (temp file creation, file watcher, feedback panel, accept command, auto-accept for autonomous) already exists and is reused — not duplicated
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  d0094d12-701d-4793-8e11-8e54a60c086d:
    id: d0094d12-701d-4793-8e11-8e54a60c086d
    content: The "no delete, no rewrite" constraint is enforced via prompt instructions only — no code-level enforcement. If the AI disobeys, the user rejects (checkpoint) or undoes (autonomous).
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  6a673406-e4e2-4afe-96a8-eef3b1b38c8e:
    id: 6a673406-e4e2-4afe-96a8-eef3b1b38c8e
    content: The context menu send path currently calls `executeInTerminalWithContext` for execute mode (fire-and-forget) and `collaborateInTerminal` for collaborate mode. Execute needs to call the collaborate pipeline with an execute-specific prompt.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  240065c5-9b88-4c6d-89f9-86c28682c161:
    id: 240065c5-9b88-4c6d-89f9-86c28682c161
    content: The workflow `sendContentToTerminal` function currently has separate paths for collaborate and execute. The execute path needs to use the collaborate pipeline instead of fire-and-forget.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  e47d89bf-349a-4ed0-b3cd-1a4b668529e6:
