  c17509e0-f9ab-492a-8707-00bb2d076174:
    id: c17509e0-f9ab-492a-8707-00bb2d076174
    content: Problem statement
    children:
      - 40b139f3-86d7-4205-9094-f88cb6b715c2
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  40b139f3-86d7-4205-9094-f88cb6b715c2:
    id: 40b139f3-86d7-4205-9094-f88cb6b715c2
    content: When a user sends content in execute mode to the browser, the content is copied to the clipboard as a fire-and-forget prompt — the AI does work but nothing comes back to the tree. The user must manually update node statuses afterward. The browser collaborate pipeline already has a round-trip mechanism (clipboard copy with structured prompt, clipboard monitor watches for the AI's response, feedback panel displays result, accept/undo). Execute mode needs the same pipeline with an execute-specific prompt — one that instructs the AI to update statuses rather than rewrite content.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  1f005394-aac7-4f45-8838-24e2e0a094df:
    id: 1f005394-aac7-4f45-8838-24e2e0a094df
    content: Use cases
    children:
      - 2c4ad01f-2797-4f2e-862c-bb452161567e
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  2c4ad01f-2797-4f2e-862c-bb452161567e:
    id: 2c4ad01f-2797-4f2e-862c-bb452161567e
    content: 'Primary: User right-clicks a node with an execute-mode context → Send to browser. Content is copied to clipboard with execute-specific instructions. User pastes into browser AI, copies the AI''s response. Clipboard monitor detects the response, feedback panel opens for review. User accepts or cancels.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
