  8a29436b-6492-496f-846b-1b27cc024b1b:
    id: 8a29436b-6492-496f-846b-1b27cc024b1b
    content: The panel store keeps its global state for layout (panelPosition, panelHeight, panelWidth) but manages activeContent and previousContent per-file via a map keyed by file path
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  6327e856-ffd6-45ee-8c3b-63f2e7a918e8:
    id: 6327e856-ffd6-45ee-8c3b-63f2e7a918e8
    content: All store methods (showTerminal, showBrowser, showFeedback, closeFeedback, hidePanel) receive the active file path implicitly (from the store's own tracking of which file is active) and operate on that file's entry in the map
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  09ef025d-cf28-4663-842a-8e17af22554a:
    id: 09ef025d-cf28-4663-842a-8e17af22554a
    content: On file tab switch, the store's active file reference updates, which causes all subscribers to re-render with the new file's panel state
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  819cda77-a0ac-4b9b-9d87-2586edafe0f8:
    id: 819cda77-a0ac-4b9b-9d87-2586edafe0f8
    content: Zoom tab file paths are resolved to their parent file path before any panel state lookup — a helper already exists in storeManager (parseZoomPath)
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  a50916bb-77ec-48c0-83b0-9f912b8c1afe:
    id: a50916bb-77ec-48c0-83b0-9f912b8c1afe
    content: 'The 27 consumer files fall into two categories: those that read activeContent (must now read from the per-file map) and those that only read layout (panelPosition/Height/Width — no change needed). The store''s public API stays the same — consumers don''t need to pass file path, they just call showTerminal() etc. and the store internally routes to the correct file.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  82012a8e-3331-4b90-a0d2-68a2ed31a2b6:
