  85d3eba0-e1e7-4e56-82e4-03bd23a8aff2:
    id: 85d3eba0-e1e7-4e56-82e4-03bd23a8aff2
    content: 'Highest likelihood of defects: Zustand re-render behavior when activeContent is computed from the map. If the selector doesn''t detect a change (same reference), the panel won''t update on tab switch. This must be tested with actual React rendering, not just store unit tests.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  8d5485d3-8e64-4a0a-9aa6-a3972cb5997a:
    id: 8d5485d3-8e64-4a0a-9aa6-a3972cb5997a
    content: 'Highest impact if failed: panel shows the wrong file''s content after switching tabs. User sees terminal output for the wrong project. This is the core behavior — if it doesn''t work, the entire per-file panel feature fails.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  f0ae5016-8fd2-4ec3-b6e9-5f51f22ba2e7:
    id: f0ae5016-8fd2-4ec3-b6e9-5f51f22ba2e7
    content: 'Session persistence backward compatibility: if the old format isn''t handled, users upgrading from the previous version will lose their panel state on first launch.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  1cf7c8ff-3ec6-4460-8d5e-acbe876e4e7e:
    id: 1cf7c8ff-3ec6-4460-8d5e-acbe876e4e7e
    content: The browserStore's duplicate layout state may cause unexpected behavior if panelPosition changes go through that store instead of panelStore during testing.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
