  c974e58e-d69e-495c-afb3-92745aee8360:
    id: c974e58e-d69e-495c-afb3-92745aee8360
    content: The isBrowserVisible flag may cause confusion — it's set by addTab and toggleBrowserVisibility but panel visibility is now controlled by panelStore. If components still read isBrowserVisible, they may see stale state. Audit consumers of this flag.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  e66aa818-418f-4273-82b2-0bd3399586c9:
    id: e66aa818-418f-4273-82b2-0bd3399586c9
    content: The duplicate panelPosition/panelHeight/panelWidth in browserStore vs panelStore — if components read browser-specific layout, they'll get global values which is correct. No action needed but worth noting for future cleanup.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  ff76edee-5e9f-49c9-8ead-9edcaa872272:
    id: ff76edee-5e9f-49c9-8ead-9edcaa872272
    content: Browser tabs don't have external processes, so cleanup is simpler than terminals — just removing entries from the map. No PTY processes to kill, no confirmation dialog needed.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  22a0d447-dada-4b25-87af-1b423f3edf37:
    id: 22a0d447-dada-4b25-87af-1b423f3edf37
    content: The addTab method currently calls showBrowser() on isBrowserVisible — this should continue to work if it sets isBrowserVisible for the current file's entry. But the actual panel visibility is controlled by panelStore.showBrowser(). Need to ensure both are called or consolidate.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
