  6420571b-3446-4a37-a2d7-30d0cdea82cc:
    id: 6420571b-3446-4a37-a2d7-30d0cdea82cc
    content: There is an existing constraint where only one non automated collaboration can be in progress within a file - if it's terminal or browser
    children:
      - 1b398539-bac9-4cf8-8c8b-9c2caba7d911
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  1b398539-bac9-4cf8-8c8b-9c2caba7d911:
    id: 1b398539-bac9-4cf8-8c8b-9c2caba7d911
    content: Basically, if the user hasn't accepted the feedback in the feedback panel within a file, they can't start another collaboration
    children:
      - 65ddf934-d3ec-486e-b261-acc04325a16f
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  65ddf934-d3ec-486e-b261-acc04325a16f:
    id: 65ddf934-d3ec-486e-b261-acc04325a16f
    content: We should continue to respect that
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  c55ad1a9-ce15-4e95-a4e3-60a1c4111fdc:
    id: c55ad1a9-ce15-4e95-a4e3-60a1c4111fdc
    content: The clipboard monitor is a single IPC channel — it cannot be multiplexed per-file.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  e2eaac5f-2a24-4294-b413-bb981c28a069:
    id: e2eaac5f-2a24-4294-b413-bb981c28a069
    content: This guard applies only to browser (clipboard-based) collaborations. Terminal (file-watcher-based) collaborations are inherently per-file.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
