  dcff58c3-d6db-4cc4-afc5-367bf04e78f5:
    id: dcff58c3-d6db-4cc4-afc5-367bf04e78f5
    content: The `collaborate` function in sendActions.ts already checks `state.collaboratingNodeId` to block concurrent collaborations within a file. This guard needs to be extended to check all stores for a browser collaboration before starting a new one.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  14e1166a-2198-4aa8-937d-5011d6faa791:
    id: 14e1166a-2198-4aa8-937d-5011d6faa791
    content: Terminal collaborations (`collaborateInTerminal`) do NOT need the cross-file guard — each uses its own temp file and file watcher, so they can run concurrently across files.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  92d034a6-cdb6-4faa-88d0-065f05a9f643:
    id: 92d034a6-cdb6-4faa-88d0-065f05a9f643
    content: The existing within-file guard (`state.collaboratingNodeId` check) remains unchanged — it already blocks any collaboration (browser or terminal) when one is in progress for that file.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  5961f1ef-64c2-4be2-a821-6912da927d7b:
    id: 5961f1ef-64c2-4be2-a821-6912da927d7b
    content: The cross-file guard only applies to browser collaborations. It checks `storeManager.getAllStores()` for any store with an active `collaboratingNodeId` where the collaboration source is browser (clipboard-based).
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  5d8c32e5-2f28-4421-af91-19d7e24612d2:
    id: 5d8c32e5-2f28-4421-af91-19d7e24612d2
    content: 'The guard needs to distinguish between browser and terminal collaborations. Currently `collaboratingNodeId` doesn''t track the source. Options: (a) add a `collaborationSource: ''browser'' | ''terminal'' | null` field to the tree store, or (b) check whether any clipboard monitor is active via a flag on the panel/feedback state.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
