  42265b71-3b8d-445f-b9ab-f61434448281:
    id: 42265b71-3b8d-445f-b9ab-f61434448281
    content: Risks and edge cases
    children:
      - 434a3c2f-f249-48c4-8e9e-a709d2b56a9f
      - fdbd309e-e850-45b3-b540-5f78e7ddedc1
      - f0542942-f7e0-4845-a325-bbee4b2ee0e9
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  434a3c2f-f249-48c4-8e9e-a709d2b56a9f:
    id: 434a3c2f-f249-48c4-8e9e-a709d2b56a9f
    content: 'Race condition: user clicks "Send to browser" on two files rapidly before the first clipboard monitor starts. The guard should be synchronous (it reads store state directly) so both checks happen in the same event loop tick — the first sets collaboratingNodeId, the second sees it and blocks. This should work naturally since Zustand state updates are synchronous.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  fdbd309e-e850-45b3-b540-5f78e7ddedc1:
    id: fdbd309e-e850-45b3-b540-5f78e7ddedc1
    content: 'File close with active browser collaboration: the collaboration metadata survives in the saved file, but the clipboard monitor stops (the hook unmounts). If the file is reopened, `restoreCollaborationState` restores the `collaboratingNodeId` but the `collaborationSource` needs to also be restored (or inferred).'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  f0542942-f7e0-4845-a325-bbee4b2ee0e9:
    id: f0542942-f7e0-4845-a325-bbee4b2ee0e9
    content: The `collaborationSource` field adds a new piece of state to the tree store. It must be non-persisted (not saved to the .arbo file) — it's runtime state only. On restore, the collaboration should be treated as needing re-classification (the user would re-send to continue).
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
