  f0f61485-b3c3-4a35-a34b-9c98c13fde92:
    id: f0f61485-b3c3-4a35-a34b-9c98c13fde92
    content: Risks
    children:
      - 7700d853-8a49-4278-8260-18d35e088b9d
      - e5f0da32-5bb2-4a3d-bb8c-a70229433003
      - 8ce89250-fc5d-4e47-b38d-b82d7d1fe078
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  7700d853-8a49-4278-8260-18d35e088b9d:
    id: 7700d853-8a49-4278-8260-18d35e088b9d
    content: 'Highest likelihood of defects: the collaborationSource not being cleared in all exit paths (finishAccept, finishCancel, cancelCollaboration, file close). If any path misses the clear, the guard becomes permanently blocking. The lifecycle tests must cover all exit paths.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  e5f0da32-5bb2-4a3d-bb8c-a70229433003:
    id: e5f0da32-5bb2-4a3d-bb8c-a70229433003
    content: 'Highest impact if failed: the guard not firing at all, allowing two browser collaborations to compete for the clipboard. The clipboard monitor would route the response to whichever store it finds first — likely the wrong one. This corrupts the feedback.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  8ce89250-fc5d-4e47-b38d-b82d7d1fe078:
    id: 8ce89250-fc5d-4e47-b38d-b82d7d1fe078
    content: The collaborationSource field is runtime-only and not persisted. On app restart, a restored collaboration has no source. This means the guard won't block on restored collaborations — acceptable since the clipboard monitor isn't running either (it starts fresh on re-send).
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  ef65feec-84bc-43e4-bd05-6a9ee1aea626:
