  8912f9b0-7f3c-48e2-a121-69dd99f29831:
    id: 8912f9b0-7f3c-48e2-a121-69dd99f29831
    content: 'Highest likelihood of defects: the useTabIndicators hook performance — subscribing to multiple stores with multiple selectors. If subscriptions aren''t carefully scoped, every state change in any file''s store could re-render the entire tab bar. The hook must use stable selectors and memoize the output.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  49405650-3143-411e-955f-a61704f61b8d:
    id: 49405650-3143-411e-955f-a61704f61b8d
    content: 'Highest impact if failed: indicators stuck permanently (state not clearing) or never appearing (subscription not firing). Both would undermine the feature''s core value. The clear-on-state-change tests are critical.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  cfb1fadf-237b-42ee-8386-b916cfed8e75:
    id: cfb1fadf-237b-42ee-8386-b916cfed8e75
    content: The "action required" definition may evolve — currently it's awaiting-validation OR feedback pending. If the definition changes, the hook logic and tests need updating. This should be clearly defined before implementation.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  edd7509a-dfac-4f81-b6e5-8524ad871db0:
    id: edd7509a-dfac-4f81-b6e5-8524ad871db0
    content: The toast for non-active feedback fires from useFeedbackClipboard which is a React hook — it only runs when the component is mounted. If the feedback panel component isn't mounted (e.g. the panel is hidden), the toast may not fire. Need to verify the feedback processing path runs regardless of panel visibility.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
