  d8e4cd42-4c23-42e5-b9e4-786339ca09f7:
    id: d8e4cd42-4c23-42e5-b9e4-786339ca09f7
    content: When a file tab is closed, its panel resources (terminals, browser tabs) need to be cleaned up. Currently closing a file only cleans up the tree store. With per-file panels, closing a file must also stop running terminals and remove browser tabs. Pending feedback survives file close — the collaboration state is persisted in node metadata and the temp file on disk, and restores automatically when the file is reopened (same behavior as app restart).
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
