  bafcd782-5962-45e7-982b-bc8cdef7b7bc:
    id: bafcd782-5962-45e7-982b-bc8cdef7b7bc
    content: 'Race condition: user starts a workflow while the confirmation dialog is showing. The dialog was shown because of an existing workflow. If a new workflow starts between dialog show and user confirm, it should also be stopped on close.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  0ed80dfd-dc79-455b-8206-8233c3c7e2a7:
    id: 0ed80dfd-dc79-455b-8206-8233c3c7e2a7
    content: Terminal PTY kill may take time — closeFileTerminals is async. The close should await it before proceeding to save. If a PTY doesn't respond to kill, it should time out gracefully.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  5eef43ed-f300-4145-b500-3b259127b264:
    id: 5eef43ed-f300-4145-b500-3b259127b264
    content: The existing unsaved changes dialog (for temporary files) runs BEFORE the workflow check. If a temp file has both unsaved changes AND a running workflow, the user sees two dialogs in sequence. This is acceptable but could be combined into a single dialog for better UX (enhancement, not blocker).
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  565c8ee3-b84c-48d4-a1bb-04b43bd2209a:
    id: 565c8ee3-b84c-48d4-a1bb-04b43bd2209a
    content: Closing a file with an active browser collaboration needs to stop the clipboard monitor, but the monitor is managed by the useFeedbackClipboard React hook. If the hook unmounts (panel hides on close), the monitor stops automatically via the cleanup effect. Verify this happens naturally.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: abandoned
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
