  43ea2417-0b22-4d60-9997-e47414aa2143:
    id: 43ea2417-0b22-4d60-9997-e47414aa2143
    content: 'Explicit-only contexts: remove auto-apply of default contexts'
    children:
      - 8dc0339d-a6a5-4854-8922-4761e26d2381
      - 748993b5-f9e8-4eff-93c8-2bc7f33523a3
      - 614359e6-73dd-4316-8af4-0e6e36397ab2
      - b87ed072-5d61-4345-a96f-274fd7601355
      - d7a04d68-f6f4-47db-80d2-2df4aa964045
      - cb466d4d-7501-475c-85c0-cee4cabecf9a
      - ae47740d-2ce0-4055-b764-303d045c82ad
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: false
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  8dc0339d-a6a5-4854-8922-4761e26d2381:
    id: 8dc0339d-a6a5-4854-8922-4761e26d2381
    content: Problem statement
    children:
      - 74f3ca2a-c88b-4df7-a02e-e8fb9cae8abc
      - 6adeb6a3-2a66-49e0-99de-220f95bc1204
      - 53a74df8-a662-4058-8f3b-fa6b1fed32bf
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  74f3ca2a-c88b-4df7-a02e-e8fb9cae8abc:
    id: 74f3ca2a-c88b-4df7-a02e-e8fb9cae8abc
    content: 'Role: any user who sends node content to an AI (via terminal or browser)'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  6adeb6a3-2a66-49e0-99de-220f95bc1204:
    id: 6adeb6a3-2a66-49e0-99de-220f95bc1204
    content: 'Current experience: when no context is explicitly applied, a built-in default ("Basic review" or "Basic execution") is silently wrapped around the node''s content before it is sent. This hidden wrapping surprises users who want to send a node''s own instructions directly (e.g. a reusable blueprint node describing a git-commit procedure) because the default framing conflicts with the node''s intent'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  53a74df8-a662-4058-8f3b-fa6b1fed32bf:
    id: 53a74df8-a662-4058-8f3b-fa6b1fed32bf
    content: 'Why insufficient: the hidden auto-apply violates the predictable-behavior principle. Users have to reason about an invisible default, and reusable "action-like" nodes (blueprint content meant to be sent as-is) cannot be used cleanly without a workaround'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  748993b5-f9e8-4eff-93c8-2bc7f33523a3:
    id: 748993b5-f9e8-4eff-93c8-2bc7f33523a3
    content: Use cases
    children:
      - e3ac5972-d318-469a-8a99-1486af4674d8
      - 31c65899-8972-4b7d-a449-68d5a80eef26
      - dde73db1-3029-4290-8cd0-b0950f91901d
      - 08eb2781-f905-479f-834f-bae9bafe00f6
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  e3ac5972-d318-469a-8a99-1486af4674d8:
    id: e3ac5972-d318-469a-8a99-1486af4674d8
    content: 'Primary (happy path): user creates a blueprint node containing reusable instructions, sends the node to the terminal, and the AI receives exactly the node''s content with no additional wrapping'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  31c65899-8972-4b7d-a449-68d5a80eef26:
    id: 31c65899-8972-4b7d-a449-68d5a80eef26
    content: 'Secondary: user wants the old wrapping behavior — they explicitly apply "Basic review" or "Basic execution" from the Apply-context submenu at the relevant node (or at the root for tree-wide effect). Inheritance carries it to descendants as today'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  dde73db1-3029-4290-8cd0-b0950f91901d:
    id: dde73db1-3029-4290-8cd0-b0950f91901d
    content: 'Alternative: user runs a workflow step on a node with no context applied anywhere on the ancestor chain — the step sends the node''s content bare, same rule as manual send'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  08eb2781-f905-479f-834f-bae9bafe00f6:
    id: 08eb2781-f905-479f-834f-bae9bafe00f6
    content: 'Alternative: user opens an existing .arbo file that never had a context applied — sends now go bare. User can opt into the previous behavior by applying a default at the root'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  614359e6-73dd-4316-8af4-0e6e36397ab2:
