  09b66b45-66a4-455e-917c-b8d66710231e:
    id: 09b66b45-66a4-455e-917c-b8d66710231e
    content: Sending a node with no context applied anywhere on its ancestor chain sends only the node's rendered content to the AI — no default context wrapping
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  d8d6105e-56d3-455f-b427-fb38746b5d63:
    id: d8d6105e-56d3-455f-b427-fb38746b5d63
    content: The built-in defaults ("Basic review", "Basic execution") remain available in the Apply-context submenu and can be applied explicitly at any node, overriding any inherited context exactly like a user-defined context would
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  3fc1068c-8741-44d9-8ab3-1e83d2b739d7:
    id: 3fc1068c-8741-44d9-8ab3-1e83d2b739d7
    content: 'Existing inheritance rules are unchanged: a context applied at an ancestor inherits to all descendants unless a descendant applies its own different context'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  8537f112-55e7-4e05-b383-886518903ace:
    id: 8537f112-55e7-4e05-b383-886518903ace
    content: 'Workflow steps follow the same rule: a step sends what the applicable context specifies (its own, or inherited). Steps have no separate auto-apply'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  7bf8cddb-8fc1-4e02-b50b-e097ee4f6723:
    id: 7bf8cddb-8fc1-4e02-b50b-e097ee4f6723
    content: The Send menu displays a tooltip or hover hint of the form "No context applied — AI receives only node content" when no context resolves up the ancestor chain
    children: []
