      plugins: {}
  f7106618-6743-4173-938e-05fe2dddb225:
    id: f7106618-6743-4173-938e-05fe2dddb225
    content: Complications
    children:
      - d4b6cce8-eb4f-4732-ba8a-5b9e62e44ae7
      - 319e1a12-bcf2-445b-a8fd-ab11217bd821
      - 28580e48-bac4-470c-947c-3a247fc9f931
      - cd68f07a-7dd8-4455-92ec-6d7741ae948c
      - 964d5ce6-4e77-4903-b78d-d2d3cf481cf4
      - c46a03dd-5a03-4da3-aab0-8df457d219bc
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  d4b6cce8-eb4f-4732-ba8a-5b9e62e44ae7:
    id: d4b6cce8-eb4f-4732-ba8a-5b9e62e44ae7
    content: 'Two distinct symptoms that may or may not share a cause: (a) activeNodeId (keyboard focus) shifts to the advanced node, (b) the view scrolls to it. Fixing one does not guarantee the other — need to trace both back independently and remove each surgically.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  319e1a12-bcf2-445b-a8fd-ab11217bd821:
    id: 319e1a12-bcf2-445b-a8fd-ab11217bd821
    content: 'Unknown trigger for the focus steal: advanceNode itself does not call selectNode, so something else (a subscription in a component, a visual-effect side effect, or a flashNode-driven scroll that also sets focus) is doing it. Impl must grep for selectNode / setActiveNodeId callers that react to workflow state changes.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  28580e48-bac4-470c-947c-3a247fc9f931:
    id: 28580e48-bac4-470c-947c-3a247fc9f931
    content: 'Unknown trigger for the scroll: flashNode likely sets flashingNodeIds but does not inherently scroll. The tree view may auto-scroll flashing nodes into view as a visibility convenience — if so, the same hook is what needs to be exempted (or gated) for auto-advance.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  cd68f07a-7dd8-4455-92ec-6d7741ae948c:
    id: cd68f07a-7dd8-4455-92ec-6d7741ae948c
    content: 'Not every auto-advance should stay silent: a user actively watching their workflow progress does want to see where it has moved. The mitigation must distinguish "user is watching" from "user has moved on". Cheapest proxy: if the currently-focused node is already within the workflow subtree, keep the scroll/flash visible; if the user is focused elsewhere, do not disrupt.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  964d5ce6-4e77-4903-b78d-d2d3cf481cf4:
    id: 964d5ce6-4e77-4903-b78d-d2d3cf481cf4
    content: 'Data-loss risk is real: per the user, keystrokes meant for a different node silently land on the advanced one because activeNodeId changed mid-type. This is the acute symptom — even if we keep the flash, the keystroke hijack must be prevented first.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  c46a03dd-5a03-4da3-aab0-8df457d219bc:
    id: c46a03dd-5a03-4da3-aab0-8df457d219bc
    content: 'Out of scope: redesigning workflow status notifications, adding a "follow workflow" toggle in preferences, changing toast frequency or wording, and altering the flash animation itself.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  2003956d-2a9a-421f-8f7a-467af0a69fce:
    id: 2003956d-2a9a-421f-8f7a-467af0a69fce
    content: Approach
    children:
      - 1e8ba662-2b46-4742-a4d4-388ecab89cf2
      - 0691102d-9bc4-4d22-af89-29c95fbfba95
      - cb312040-70c2-4483-9083-355afd73b8cc
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  1e8ba662-2b46-4742-a4d4-388ecab89cf2:
    id: 1e8ba662-2b46-4742-a4d4-388ecab89cf2
    content: Remove activeNodeId changes from the auto-advance path. The flash (visual indicator) and toast (existing notification) are enough to communicate progress without stealing keyboard focus. advanceNode must not mutate activeNodeId directly or indirectly.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  0691102d-9bc4-4d22-af89-29c95fbfba95:
    id: 0691102d-9bc4-4d22-af89-29c95fbfba95
    content: Gate the scroll-into-view behavior so it only triggers for auto-advance when the currently-focused node is already inside the same workflow subtree. When the user is focused elsewhere, skip the scroll — they are working on something else and do not want the viewport jerked.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  cb312040-70c2-4483-9083-355afd73b8cc:
    id: cb312040-70c2-4483-9083-355afd73b8cc
    content: 'Non-obvious: user-initiated advance (continueWorkflow after a checkpoint) should keep the old focus/scroll behavior — the user just clicked "Continue" and expects the view to follow. The gate must be on auto-advance specifically, not on all advanceNode calls. Differentiator: whether advanceNode was called from handleHookEvent (auto) vs continueWorkflow (user-initiated).'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  0ca1eb57-09a6-4926-81a9-882aec9e0319:
    id: 0ca1eb57-09a6-4926-81a9-882aec9e0319
    content: Happens when there are a lot of available contexts
    children:
      - d2d3a434-80c4-46a1-9fdb-1d66b535329e
      - 8bcbec79-e563-4da5-b239-08a6bf96b12d
