      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  540e7fe7-0d70-4333-a38c-38902ecd7069:
    id: 540e7fe7-0d70-4333-a38c-38902ecd7069
    content: And we need to calculate window position and cut off and sub menu height better to correctly place the sub menu dynamically
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  f2a0083e-e329-4d2f-b5cf-55f4a53120ab:
    id: f2a0083e-e329-4d2f-b5cf-55f4a53120ab
    content: Technical refinement
    children:
      - 1c69eb4a-731b-4660-ab0c-35441d16cb60
      - ce9a4869-ef66-407a-b288-b50a0b6a46a7
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  1c69eb4a-731b-4660-ab0c-35441d16cb60:
    id: 1c69eb4a-731b-4660-ab0c-35441d16cb60
    content: Complications
    children:
      - fb7761cc-18b5-4715-9929-dd431d317d84
      - 1c400867-cd64-4417-8eb6-00304b402b37
      - c91afdf6-7e7c-4bad-bc2c-3b312c5246a7
      - 831ce142-7688-4e01-82f2-09f80463b5d5
      - 1c5499f3-c259-4563-b850-5a4cdee5d8a4
      - 83c97406-34b2-4f07-92ab-bb36777c6c14
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  fb7761cc-18b5-4715-9929-dd431d317d84:
    id: fb7761cc-18b5-4715-9929-dd431d317d84
    content: 'ContextMenu primitive has no column support today. ContextMenuItem is a flat shape (label, icon, onClick, separator, disabled). A side-by-side two-column layout requires either a new item variant (e.g. `{ columns: [ContextMenuItem[], ContextMenuItem[]] }`) or a dedicated renderer — either way it touches a UI primitive shared across the app, not just the context submenu. Ripple risk.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  1c400867-cd64-4417-8eb6-00304b402b37:
    id: 1c400867-cd64-4417-8eb6-00304b402b37
    content: Columns only delay truncation, they do not eliminate it. If a user has many contexts on both sides, the tallest column still sets the menu height. The dynamic positioning fix is load-bearing regardless of whether columns ship.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  c91afdf6-7e7c-4bad-bc2c-3b312c5246a7:
    id: c91afdf6-7e7c-4bad-bc2c-3b312c5246a7
    content: Submenu positioning is not like a top-level popup. The submenu opens relative to its parent menu's trigger item, so flipping direction (up instead of down, or left instead of right) has to track the parent's edge and the target item's position within the parent. More complex than placing a standalone menu at cursor coords.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  831ce142-7688-4e01-82f2-09f80463b5d5:
    id: 831ce142-7688-4e01-82f2-09f80463b5d5
    content: Column layout breaks linear keyboard nav. Current up/down arrow handling walks a flat list; with two columns, arrow semantics become 2D (left/right to switch column) and radio-group selection semantics for "which is the active context" need re-thinking. Non-trivial input work attached to the columns idea.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  1c5499f3-c259-4563-b850-5a4cdee5d8a4:
    id: 1c5499f3-c259-4563-b850-5a4cdee5d8a4
    content: 'Measure-then-place dance is fragile. Dynamic positioning typically renders the menu invisibly, measures, then repositions — which can cause a one-frame flicker or layout shift. Options: useLayoutEffect reposition pass, or rely on max-height + overflow-y: auto as a defensive fallback so the worst case scrolls instead of clips.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  83c97406-34b2-4f07-92ab-bb36777c6c14:
    id: 83c97406-34b2-4f07-92ab-bb36777c6c14
    content: 'Out of scope: search/filter for contexts, pagination, collapsible sections, replacing the ContextMenu component with a third-party library (radix, react-menu). Any of those is a separate feature discussion.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  ce9a4869-ef66-407a-b288-b50a0b6a46a7:
    id: ce9a4869-ef66-407a-b288-b50a0b6a46a7
    content: Approach
    children:
      - 87b07e91-5bd7-4520-b290-dbf912434a68
      - 754d41a5-305f-4cda-b525-a3bc894060d6
      - fea576d5-0175-4430-be19-f0710fa27458
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  87b07e91-5bd7-4520-b290-dbf912434a68:
    id: 87b07e91-5bd7-4520-b290-dbf912434a68
    content: 'Ship the positioning fix first and independently. Detect when the submenu would clip the viewport (top or bottom) and reposition — flip upward if the natural-down direction clips, and add a max-height + overflow-y: auto fallback so extreme cases scroll instead of disappear. Change lives in the ContextMenu/submenu positioning logic, not in useSetContextSubmenu.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  754d41a5-305f-4cda-b525-a3bc894060d6:
    id: 754d41a5-305f-4cda-b525-a3bc894060d6
    content: Validate whether columns are still needed after the positioning fix lands. If scrolling + flipping covers the real-world cases the user hits, the columns refactor has poor ROI and should be deferred. If the user still experiences truncation / awkward tall menus, revisit with columns as a second, optional layer.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  fea576d5-0175-4430-be19-f0710fa27458:
    id: fea576d5-0175-4430-be19-f0710fa27458
    content: 'Non-obvious: the positioning fix is the one that actually removes the acute bug; the columns idea is an ergonomic improvement that depends on the positioning fix being correct. If we ship columns without the positioning fix, tall 2-column menus still clip. Ordering matters: positioning → evaluate → maybe columns.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  05787b3f-79c7-45aa-87df-9bc5435b523d:
