  7095c598-b8ae-4f99-954f-181cfa9df3af:
    id: 7095c598-b8ae-4f99-954f-181cfa9df3af
    content: 'Initial investigation suggests the issue is already resolved: `project.arbo` and all four `blueprints/*.arbo` files contain only UUID-style node keys except for the intentional `root` sentinel. All known ID-generation code paths use `uuidv4()` — parseMarkdown, cloneNodesWithNewIds, AcceptFeedbackCommand, PasteNodesCommand, and acceptFeedbackArchive all go through `uuid/v4`. If this is correct, the refinement collapses to "verify and close."'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  a536cc8e-1dab-444c-9da3-4c56f2a5dc60:
    id: a536cc8e-1dab-444c-9da3-4c56f2a5dc60
    content: 'ROI warning: if nothing is currently broken, adding migration logic or defensive runtime checks is speculative. Avoid building a rewrite-on-load mechanism unless real data still exhibits the bug. Over-engineering risk is high here — the user has the "we might have fixed this" uncertainty, not a reproducible failing case.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  ddd85fe5-e4c6-40c2-b51f-68d639aeafd1:
    id: ddd85fe5-e4c6-40c2-b51f-68d639aeafd1
    content: 'Files outside this checkout might still show the bug: older saved `.arbo` files, files shared by other users, or files from pre-fix versions of Arborescent. If such a file is loaded into the current app, it should load without errors (ids are just strings), but cross-references in `children` arrays rely on exact-match ids, so legacy title-based ids would continue to work in-place — there''s no silent breakage, just aesthetic oddity in YAML.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  65c6c882-2090-4e57-9ce1-31d0fe13632f:
    id: 65c6c882-2090-4e57-9ce1-31d0fe13632f
    content: The `root` sentinel is intentional and must be left alone. Any "normalize all non-UUID ids" pass has to explicitly exempt `root` (and any other reserved sentinels introduced later).
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
