    content: If the reset write to the target terminal fails, the step is marked errored and the prompt is not sent
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  973f2a25-8698-455b-a202-09691e76441b:
    id: 973f2a25-8698-455b-a202-09691e76441b
    content: If the clear-complete confirmation does not arrive within the bounded window, the reset is retried — mirroring the existing retry behaviour for an unconfirmed prompt
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  21982ae2-4968-4023-a988-47bd59cdb188:
    id: 21982ae2-4968-4023-a988-47bd59cdb188
    content: Retry cadence and maximum attempt count match the prompt-retry policy (same shape, separate counter dedicated to this step's clear attempts)
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  7295ab8a-2fa6-416a-b4e1-172184570a09:
    id: 7295ab8a-2fa6-416a-b4e1-172184570a09
    content: After the maximum retry count is exhausted without confirmation, the step is marked errored and the prompt is not sent
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  90731942-66c0-4af2-a62e-ba6a6b3f00ee:
    id: 90731942-66c0-4af2-a62e-ba6a6b3f00ee
    content: If a late confirmation arrives after a retry has already been dispatched, the step proceeds on the first confirmation and subsequent duplicates are ignored — no double-advances
    children: []
