  1c0a9402-0e5a-458c-b819-00167740f331:
    id: 1c0a9402-0e5a-458c-b819-00167740f331
    content: First step of a workflow with the flag enabled has no prior-step completion to wait on — reset must fire immediately on workflow start, not block on a non-existent Stop
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  cf8e694c-7413-45e1-a2d5-7f81a115f548:
    id: cf8e694c-7413-45e1-a2d5-7f81a115f548
    content: '`/clear` must be written to the PTY as a raw slash-command keystroke, not through any bracketed-paste or multi-line paste path used for prompt text — otherwise Claude treats the string as message content rather than as a command'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  79b2d83d-fcd0-4071-a6a4-65c93969a2ed:
    id: 79b2d83d-fcd0-4071-a6a4-65c93969a2ed
    content: 'The workflow execution state machine currently transitions advanceNode → send. This element inserts a new transient "clearing" phase: advanceNode → clearing → await-confirm → send. stopWorkflow, workflow disruption, manual pause, and any cancel paths must all recognise and cleanly exit this new state'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  7a7cf8a0-27a9-4fc4-b774-de076652dd1f:
    id: 7a7cf8a0-27a9-4fc4-b774-de076652dd1f
    content: 'Atomic remap requirement: the SessionStart source:"clear" handler must update workflowSessionMap to the new session_id *before* the post-clear prompt is written. Otherwise UserPromptSubmit / Stop for that prompt arrives with a session_id the handler''s early-return will silently drop (as unmapped)'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  9d7cd664-25c3-4ee3-bfab-14a973f4b393:
    id: 9d7cd664-25c3-4ee3-bfab-14a973f4b393
    content: workflowSessionMap grows unbounded across many clears unless the old session_id entry is actively deleted during remap
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  52ec6d44-f9f7-4782-8484-8ee29b53e874:
    id: 52ec6d44-f9f7-4782-8484-8ee29b53e874
    content: The flag is meaningful on all stepType values (manual / checkpoint / autonomous), not only autonomous — a user may reasonably want a clean session before a reviewable checkpoint or a manual step
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  1015304a-700f-47c2-974c-1ee9a4ef0695:
    id: 1015304a-700f-47c2-974c-1ee9a4ef0695
    content: If `/clear` is written to a terminal where Claude is not actually running, no SessionStart hook will ever fire — retries will exhaust and the step will error, leaving the literal text `/clear` sitting in whatever shell is there. Per user direction this is acceptable (user's responsibility), but worth naming as the failure mode
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  225d2a39-b963-4880-a591-48ce2d6c8acb:
    id: 225d2a39-b963-4880-a591-48ce2d6c8acb
    content: 'Blueprint metadata pass-through: confirm the blueprint export/import path does not use a metadata allowlist that would drop an unknown new field. If it does, the allowlist needs the new key added'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  dc82a67d-7419-4809-a92f-fec78ec0af4a:
