      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  320ffccc-77ba-440b-ac91-1e204ec52f94:
    id: 320ffccc-77ba-440b-ac91-1e204ec52f94
    content: The workflow state-machine extension (new transient "clearing" state with its own retry counter, disruption handling, and atomic session_id remap) is the single non-trivial piece. It is moderately intrusive to workflowExecutionActions, not just a hook-branch addition. Not large enough to kill the element, but the earlier "one new hook branch + one remap" framing undersold it
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  f1dcf138-0e47-4f90-ab4c-3c4ee1abf0b6:
    id: f1dcf138-0e47-4f90-ab4c-3c4ee1abf0b6
    content: Prompt-retry and clear-retry counters must be strictly separate — a successful clear followed by a lost prompt must not count against the clear's retry budget, and vice versa
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  07dc7de5-4fc7-4cc1-87b1-e85ad9caa102:
    id: 07dc7de5-4fc7-4cc1-87b1-e85ad9caa102
    content: Approach summary
