  5acc658c-f13d-4284-a37a-4c9394a6288c:
    id: 5acc658c-f13d-4284-a37a-4c9394a6288c
    content: 'Metadata + UI: add a boolean flag (e.g. `clearSession`) to NodeMetadata in src/shared/types/treeNode.ts alongside decomposition / recurse / nextStepContext / resolveLinkedContent, and render it as a checkbox in the workflow step options panel. Default off. Persists with the node; rides in blueprints'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  2d6e4745-0061-4986-a92b-971a9a2c9c84:
    id: 2d6e4745-0061-4986-a92b-971a9a2c9c84
    content: 'Runtime: extend workflowExecutionActions to interpose a "clearing" phase between step-advance and prompt-send when the flag is set. Write `/clear\n` to the step''s bound terminal (not broadcast), await confirmation, retry on timeout with the prompt-retry policy shape but a separate counter, error the step on max-retry exhaustion. Existing disruption / stop / pause paths extended to understand the new state'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  31c4b91c-c542-4fc8-8fcb-9631620af6a1:
    id: 31c4b91c-c542-4fc8-8fcb-9631620af6a1
    content: 'Hook wiring: workflowHookEventHandler.ts gains a SessionStart branch that triggers on source:"clear", atomically remaps workflowSessionMap from the old session_id to the new one (deleting the stale entry), clears the clear-retry counter, and transitions the running node from clearing → sending. Late/duplicate confirmations are idempotent'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  63b313dc-14a4-48b8-bd0d-d8ddb5b4213c:
    id: 63b313dc-14a4-48b8-bd0d-d8ddb5b4213c
    content: 'Non-obvious: (a) `/clear` must take a different send path than prompt text so Claude parses it as a slash command, not pasted content; (b) workflowSessionMap is no longer stable across a workflow''s lifetime when the flag is in use — every clear rekeys it, and every downstream handler that looks up by session_id implicitly depends on the remap having already happened'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
