  6334b0e3-573a-4ffd-9ea7-858ea946e2d4:
    id: 6334b0e3-573a-4ffd-9ea7-858ea946e2d4
    content: Implementation notes and deliberate scope limits
    children:
      - 6503e52e-98f1-4206-97bc-e0dfcb1d39cb
      - 508cc73d-a0f6-428d-8564-01807856801a
      - fec952f3-663d-4fd2-a1e4-2f43942b4b88
      - 30dce026-0553-4c4d-b703-fe88f2694088
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  6503e52e-98f1-4206-97bc-e0dfcb1d39cb:
    id: 6503e52e-98f1-4206-97bc-e0dfcb1d39cb
    content: 'Root cause identified: `findPreviousNode`/`findNextNode` used the global `rootNodeId` as their traversal boundary, so in zoom mode navigation could land `activeNodeId` on the zoomed node or one of its outside siblings — nodes with no contenteditable in the zoom DOM. After that, `getActiveNodeElement()` returns null and both the navigation service and the editing service bail out at `if (!element) return;`, leaving the browser''s contenteditable defaults to handle Enter (newline) and Arrow keys (caret-to-start/end).'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  508cc73d-a0f6-428d-8564-01807856801a:
    id: 508cc73d-a0f6-428d-8564-01807856801a
    content: 'Fix landed in 3 files: (1) `navigationActions.ts` — `moveUp`/`moveDown`/`moveBack`/`moveForward` now accept an optional `boundaryNodeId` that overrides `rootNodeId` when calling the find helpers; (2) `shared.ts` — new `getEffectiveRootNodeId()` helper that reads `activeFilePath` and returns the zoomed node''s id for `zoom://…#id` paths, else null; (3) `navigationService.ts` — computes the effective root per key event and passes it to the navigation actions.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  fec952f3-663d-4fd2-a1e4-2f43942b4b88:
    id: fec952f3-663d-4fd2-a1e4-2f43942b4b88
    content: 'Tests added: 8 unit tests in `navigationActions.test.ts` covering the new boundary behavior and backwards-compatibility when no boundary is passed; 4 unit tests in `shared.test.ts` for `getEffectiveRootNodeId`; 3 integration tests in `navigationService.test.ts` that dispatch real keyboard events against a zoom-mode DOM/path. All related test files pass (`navigationActions.test.ts`, `shared.test.ts`, `navigationService.test.ts`). Typecheck and lint pass on changed files.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  30dce026-0553-4c4d-b703-fe88f2694088:
    id: 30dce026-0553-4c4d-b703-fe88f2694088
    content: 'Deliberately out of scope (marked [-] above): direct Enter-key editing-service tests, leaf/only-node edge cases, stale-listener checks, rapid-Enter timing tests, missing-node crash tests, and a11y tests. Rationale: the Enter and caret-default symptoms are side-effects of the desynced `activeNodeId`; bounding navigation at the zoom root prevents `activeNodeId` from ever leaving the rendered subtree, which keeps `getActiveNodeElement()` non-null and so the existing Enter/editing handlers keep running as designed. Adding separate tests for each symptom would duplicate coverage of the same root cause without exercising new code paths. The a11y bullets are properties of unchanged DOM — nothing in this change alters aria attributes or focus routing.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
