  2264840e-64d8-421e-a669-e8a555cbfdc7:
    id: 2264840e-64d8-421e-a669-e8a555cbfdc7
    content: 1. http(s) URLs anywhere in node text render as clickable links and open in the system browser via shell.openExternal.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  aaaf3952-c6d8-4f49-ab62-633686dfb4e3:
    id: aaaf3952-c6d8-4f49-ab62-633686dfb4e3
    content: 2. Allowlisted URI schemes (e.g. vscode://, mailto:) render as clickable and dispatch via the OS handler; schemes outside the allowlist render as plain text.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  c8eb4610-7169-4aa1-b4a3-c0d229dfe2fc:
    id: c8eb4610-7169-4aa1-b4a3-c0d229dfe2fc
    content: 3. file:// is not on the default allowlist — it renders as plain text unless a future story adds an explicit opt-in.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  20329a6a-b10e-4628-9b51-949ccdaec09d:
    id: 20329a6a-b10e-4628-9b51-949ccdaec09d
    content: 4. Pasting a URL into a node no longer auto-converts the node into an external-hyperlink node; the URL stays as inline text. Internal node-to-node hyperlinks (linkedNodeId) are unaffected.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  71cc2ef3-d24b-4308-b188-ab28038f0818:
    id: 71cc2ef3-d24b-4308-b188-ab28038f0818
    content: 5. Inline URLs are preserved verbatim in markdown export so workflow and AI sends include them.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  abff356d-2608-4029-9e05-2ecccac6cfe1:
    id: abff356d-2608-4029-9e05-2ecccac6cfe1
    content: 6. Clicking a URL opens the link without entering node edit mode; clicking off a URL behaves exactly as before.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
