  1e204dec-466c-4ffc-9132-1dd854c95c06:
    id: 1e204dec-466c-4ffc-9132-1dd854c95c06
    content: '"At the start of a node" is too narrow — URLs occur mid-text routinely; broaden to anywhere in node content.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  0a9174d5-5937-4fed-a51f-a0f8cd5449ea:
    id: 0a9174d5-5937-4fed-a51f-a0f8cd5449ea
    content: Auto-converting any pasted URL into a hyperlink node was probably never the right default; this proposal essentially reverts it. Confirm no current flow depends on auto-hyperlinking before removing it.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  6f6e4d2a-c090-483d-9f35-17ae703af9a7:
    id: 6f6e4d2a-c090-483d-9f35-17ae703af9a7
    content: Custom URI schemes (vscode://, mailto:, etc.) cross trust boundaries — default-deny with a small allowlist rather than promising "any URI" detection.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  87b9cd05-cc16-418c-a516-9d792af30261:
    id: 87b9cd05-cc16-418c-a516-9d792af30261
    content: file:// is a particularly easy footgun when rendered alongside AI output — keep it off the allowlist.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  ab14e09e-b8bd-4eb8-9d82-c5150ee31191:
    id: ab14e09e-b8bd-4eb8-9d82-c5150ee31191
    content: Out of scope for this story — rich-text formatting beyond clickable links, link previews, and inline embeds; do not let the implementation drift into those.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  1fb5443d-1364-4928-af40-36deac3e5fe3:
    id: 1fb5443d-1364-4928-af40-36deac3e5fe3
    content: Technical refinement
    children:
      - 676b6c15-cb09-4c2a-84f9-45bb8cd150f4
      - 2baab1c3-b44a-414a-9714-100d50f26327
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  676b6c15-cb09-4c2a-84f9-45bb8cd150f4:
    id: 676b6c15-cb09-4c2a-84f9-45bb8cd150f4
    content: Complications
    children:
      - 30215fd0-050f-4191-9b01-df3cdac20f58
      - 6792c81d-dab7-4863-af40-3979f6183e46
      - 13ebbca7-9f61-4afa-8ae5-0bf75d2df1a4
      - 2c4967ed-37cc-416b-b717-f12e4ad49fdb
      - 3be8714c-61ff-4126-a774-53653980e82c
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  30215fd0-050f-4191-9b01-df3cdac20f58:
    id: 30215fd0-050f-4191-9b01-df3cdac20f58
    content: Display-vs-edit separation — anchors must render only in the read-only display path. The edit surface (contenteditable / input) must keep showing plain text, otherwise caret movement, selection, and IME composition all break around the wrapped link.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  6792c81d-dab7-4863-af40-3979f6183e46:
    id: 6792c81d-dab7-4863-af40-3979f6183e46
    content: URL boundary handling — trailing punctuation (`.`, `,`, `)`, `]`) and surrounding parentheses are easy to capture into the link target by accident. Strip trailing terminators from the matched substring before opening.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  13ebbca7-9f61-4afa-8ae5-0bf75d2df1a4:
    id: 13ebbca7-9f61-4afa-8ae5-0bf75d2df1a4
    content: Drag-to-reorder conflict — nodes are draggable, so an anchor click within the drag handle area can race the drag-start handler. The anchor click path must short-circuit drag-start without breaking selection on non-link clicks.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  2c4967ed-37cc-416b-b717-f12e4ad49fdb:
    id: 2c4967ed-37cc-416b-b717-f12e4ad49fdb
    content: Clipboard fidelity — selecting and copying a node containing inline URLs must yield plain text (the original URL string), not the rendered `<a>` HTML. Paste targets outside the app should receive what the user sees, not anchor markup.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  3be8714c-61ff-4126-a774-53653980e82c:
    id: 3be8714c-61ff-4126-a774-53653980e82c
    content: Out of scope — link previews, OpenGraph fetching, inline embeds, and "smart paste" of non-URL content. Do not let scheme allowlisting drift into a generic protocol-handler framework.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  2baab1c3-b44a-414a-9714-100d50f26327:
    id: 2baab1c3-b44a-414a-9714-100d50f26327
    content: Approach summary
    children:
      - 55b68df2-068a-4bd7-904c-d6632e360bfd
      - 1748369b-d9a1-4fb5-8837-5c9eedb47c67
      - 8a999de9-b65d-4c65-a5ad-8efd386d4702
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  55b68df2-068a-4bd7-904c-d6632e360bfd:
    id: 55b68df2-068a-4bd7-904c-d6632e360bfd
    content: Render-only overlay — detect URLs and allowlisted URI schemes in node display rendering and wrap them in anchors that dispatch through the existing shell.openExternal IPC. The node stays a plain-text node; no schema or storage change.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  1748369b-d9a1-4fb5-8837-5c9eedb47c67:
    id: 1748369b-d9a1-4fb5-8837-5c9eedb47c67
    content: Paste behaviour shrinks, not grows — remove the auto-hyperlink path for external URLs only; internal node-to-node hyperlink creation (linkedNodeId) is untouched, so existing files and link semantics are preserved.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  8a999de9-b65d-4c65-a5ad-8efd386d4702:
    id: 8a999de9-b65d-4c65-a5ad-8efd386d4702
    content: Non-obvious for reviewers — the detection runs in the display renderer, never inside the editable surface. That separation is the load-bearing constraint; if it leaks, every keystroke around a URL becomes a bug report.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  5b9ab485-7fed-43e5-bf57-a49eb2ea5112:
