    content: 'Migration mapping for legacy `''execute''`: today''s Execute mode does code changes AND list updates, so the literal mapping `''execute''` → `(false, true)` (Execute-only) would silently regress observable behaviour. The behaviour-preserving mapping is `''execute''` → `(true, true)` (Both-on); legacy ''collaborate'' / absent stays `(true, false)`. Built-in `BASIC_EXECUTE_CONTEXT_ID` correspondingly resolves to `(true, true)` to match its current semantic. This PR proceeds on that resolution unless told otherwise — flag if you''d prefer the literal mapping'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  57a71fc6-25dc-43b8-b7ba-f5b803e1cfa8:
