  2091687f-20c0-4154-8fc1-7e1c39df7baa:
    id: 2091687f-20c0-4154-8fc1-7e1c39df7baa
    content: 'Context: contexts today expose a single `metadata.contextMode` (''collaborate'' | ''execute'', default ''collaborate'') that conflates two output-shape requests — asking the AI for a reviewable tree update, and asking the AI for code/file changes. The binary cannot express their combination (implement AND check off cases), nor their absence (send the context as a standalone instruction with no scaffolding and no node content)'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  bab94865-5243-4c8a-8d3c-dd51bc702d76:
    id: bab94865-5243-4c8a-8d3c-dd51bc702d76
    content: 'User: any user driving the AI from a node — running terminal executes, refining the outline, implementing-and-checking-off, or sending an instruction-only prompt with attached context'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  0f7a00d1-3c5c-4a6c-85b4-31548ec0907a:
    id: 0f7a00d1-3c5c-4a6c-85b4-31548ec0907a
    content: 'Current experience: the feedback panel auto-opens unconditionally; there is no way to ask the AI for both output shapes in one run, nor to send a free-form instruction without one of the two shapes being implied'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  5d3d974b-d6d6-4f3b-91c4-2e3263a92372:
    id: 5d3d974b-d6d6-4f3b-91c4-2e3263a92372
    content: 'Goal: each context independently declares whether the AI is asked for a reviewable tree update (`collaborate`) and/or for code/file changes (`execute`); the four (collaborate, execute) tuples surface as four named states (Collaborate / Execute / Collaborate & Execute / Action)'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
