      plugins: {}
  f4bf438d-c7c3-4f1f-8f7a-4720064585ae:
    id: f4bf438d-c7c3-4f1f-8f7a-4720064585ae
    content: Both-on is a prompt combination the AI has never received; if the two scaffolding blocks don't read coherently when concatenated, the AI will pick one and ignore the other — block copy needs a once-over before ship
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  157b33bd-7ee9-46d4-bdb9-2bf1c80ff741:
    id: 157b33bd-7ee9-46d4-bdb9-2bf1c80ff741
    content: Disjoint-blocks invariant has no automated lint — it's a one-time pre-merge grep. Any later edit that adds a cross-cutting rule to either block silently re-opens the conflict class; worth a line in the PR review checklist
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  7df1e74a-c043-4e83-a481-e2b63446e662:
    id: 7df1e74a-c043-4e83-a481-e2b63446e662
    content: Action mode is two suppressions in one (skip scaffolding AND drop node content); if either regresses, Action collapses into "scaffolding-off but node-content-on", which is a different user contract — assert both suppressions explicitly
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  8708c0bd-c19c-49b1-bf8f-d880ae3b27cc:
    id: 8708c0bd-c19c-49b1-bf8f-d880ae3b27cc
    content: 'Migration ordering: any reader that touches context metadata before the load-path translator runs (lazy hydration, async store init) will see legacy `contextMode` and miss the new flags; verify the load path is the single entry point'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  053360cf-dde8-45fd-b916-66d937b419a9:
