  08e37af2-18e7-4601-8a3e-addb8ea0a708:
    id: 08e37af2-18e7-4601-8a3e-addb8ea0a708
    content: 1. A context exposes two independent booleans, `collaborate` and `execute`, each defaulting to off (the Action state)
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  db481a43-81d5-44b3-850c-616b449ef3ff:
    id: db481a43-81d5-44b3-850c-616b449ef3ff
    content: 2. When `collaborate` is on, the prompt includes a scaffolding block asking the AI for a reviewable tree update; the feedback panel auto-opens on AI response
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  d2f02897-bc9d-44ac-9809-d05ccee8220f:
    id: d2f02897-bc9d-44ac-9809-d05ccee8220f
    content: 3. When `execute` is on, the prompt includes a scaffolding block asking the AI for code/file changes; this is an output-shape request, not a capability gate — Action mode can also do work if the context body directs it
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  eef0d2f8-3d4f-4f79-9b98-2ab62c55e91b:
    id: eef0d2f8-3d4f-4f79-9b98-2ab62c55e91b
    content: 4. When both are on, the two scaffolding blocks compose into a single prompt; the panel auto-opens because `collaborate` is on
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  7223e3c5-cc4a-451a-afd4-f4fb47fc1f14:
    id: 7223e3c5-cc4a-451a-afd4-f4fb47fc1f14
    content: 5. When both are off (Action), the prompt is the context body only — no scaffolding blocks, and the node content is omitted
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  98412d9b-97cb-4329-8187-a1a493642ce8:
    id: 98412d9b-97cb-4329-8187-a1a493642ce8
    content: 6. Scaffolding blocks are strictly disjoint by construction — the Execute block contains only code-change rules; the Collaborate block contains only list/temp-file rules — so the two compose without contradiction
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  74a3fc8a-3e34-4e21-bd7b-4aa02de7c136:
    id: 74a3fc8a-3e34-4e21-bd7b-4aa02de7c136
    content: 7. The picker shows two inline checkboxes in `CustomizeDialog` (replacing `ModeToggle`); copy frames Action as the default and Collaborate / Execute as additive output-shape requests
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  597e757b-17eb-4761-a91e-c6343ee1c23c:
    id: 597e757b-17eb-4761-a91e-c6343ee1c23c
    content: 8. The right-click apply-context menu lists the four named states (Collaborate / Execute / Collaborate & Execute / Action), each mapped to a (collaborate, execute) tuple
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  8dba79c1-14dd-4b78-b4a1-84e773639779:
    id: 8dba79c1-14dd-4b78-b4a1-84e773639779
    content: 9. Legacy `metadata.contextMode` is migrated on load — `'collaborate'` (or absent) → `(true, false)`; `'execute'` → `(false, true)`. The legacy field is dropped on next save; older app versions reading newer files fall back to defaults
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  9fbc4938-22ec-4fa5-bbac-95e8d531daf8:
    id: 9fbc4938-22ec-4fa5-bbac-95e8d531daf8
    content: 10. Only two built-in contexts ship — Basic review = `(true, false)`, Basic execute = `(false, true)`. Both-on and Action are user-composed via the picker
    children: []
