  33ee8487-ac64-4850-8904-13690596e957:
    id: 33ee8487-ac64-4850-8904-13690596e957
    content: 'PR2 worktree initially didn''t have PR1''s data layer because PR1 isn''t committed yet — git worktree forks from the last committed commit, not the working tree. To unblock PR2 work I rsynced PR1''s full source tree (`src/`) from `Arborescent-context-flags` into `Arborescent-context-picker`, then layered PR2''s picker changes on top. **When you commit PR1 and then layer PR2 on top, the rsynced PR1 portion will collide cleanly with the real PR1 commit — `git diff PR1-branch HEAD` on PR2''s worktree should yield only PR2-specific changes.** Practically: after PR1 lands, you can either (a) reset PR2''s branch to PR1''s HEAD and re-apply only the PR2-specific files, or (b) cherry-pick PR2''s deltas via the file list below.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  9b127673-430b-44ac-85f1-55e66d31e863:
    id: 9b127673-430b-44ac-85f1-55e66d31e863
