  f3f1d1ac-bcb5-4049-bbd2-3bcce13ec62c:
    id: f3f1d1ac-bcb5-4049-bbd2-3bcce13ec62c
    content: 'Inconsistency flagged: the **Apply context** right-click submenu (`useSetContextSubmenu`) groups available contexts as `c.collaborate && !c.execute` (Collaborate) and `c.execute` (Execute). Action contexts (both flags off) match neither filter and are silently dropped from that submenu — so a user can declare an Action context but cannot then apply it to another branch from this menu. The Acceptance Criteria item "All four named states are reachable from the picker, the right-click apply menu, and any keyboard shortcut wired to apply context" is therefore not fully satisfied for already-declared Action contexts. The contexts.md update notes that the Apply submenu is grouped Collaborate / Execute (with both-on contexts surfacing under Execute) but does not promise Action contexts appear there. Worth a small follow-up either to surface Action contexts under a third group or to drop the Apply menu''s mode-grouping in favour of a flat list.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
