  fbd7aac0-c7d7-4d12-889d-13985f1b3039:
    id: fbd7aac0-c7d7-4d12-889d-13985f1b3039
    content: 🔧 Implementation proposal
    children:
      - 87ad5c31-37f9-488a-bca5-0562eec3abf2
      - 9bda6dbf-64b3-420b-8e24-a28e652daf2b
      - 3af0d778-548b-4b13-86e8-fc219f81dfbf
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  87ad5c31-37f9-488a-bca5-0562eec3abf2:
    id: 87ad5c31-37f9-488a-bca5-0562eec3abf2
    content: Approach — Add a reconciliation utility that runs in the feedback panel on open and a narrower update path while the panel is open. Use `diff`'s `diffArrays` (or `fast-array-diff`) for the per-level LCS over child arrays with a content-equality comparator; equal runs are unchanged anchors, and within the gaps between anchors match by relative position to identify modified pairs (UUID inherited from the prior counterpart) plus leftover added and removed nodes. Recurse into unchanged and modified pairs to diff their children. In decomposition mode, skip the diff and mark every output node as added with a fresh UUID. While the panel is open, a text edit triggers a single per-node compare on edit commit; only structural edits re-run LCS, and only at the affected sibling level. Hold the merged subtree, per-node classifications, and the removed-list on a feedback panel view model that is persisted alongside the panel so a save/reload restores the same state; on accept the view model collapses into a single store action that writes the merged subtree and clears the panel record.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
