  117e9ccc-9df6-49a6-a8ac-fc0d3f611e97:
    id: 117e9ccc-9df6-49a6-a8ac-fc0d3f611e97
    content: Within-gap pairing can mis-inherit UUIDs — when an LCS gap holds a prior node and a new node at the same relative position whose contents are semantically unrelated (model rewrote a slot wholesale), the algorithm will mark it modified and reuse the prior UUID. Acceptable because UUID is identity and the user can still see the blue highlight, but reviewers will ask.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  f4e530cc-61ee-4432-8f32-1ea7f869e1fc:
    id: f4e530cc-61ee-4432-8f32-1ea7f869e1fc
    content: Recursion amplifies that effect — once a parent is classified modified, its children are diffed against the prior parent's children, so a wholesale rewrite at one level can cascade UUID retention into deeper subtrees.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  5146bb8f-a818-4f0b-9469-4017b5a5a94e:
