  3dc2cdfc-156e-478d-b5fc-5f29acc38b61:
    id: 3dc2cdfc-156e-478d-b5fc-5f29acc38b61
    content: 'Shipped: `findNextDecomposedSibling(stepId, nodes, executionStates)` in `src/renderer/utils/workflowHelpers.ts`. The 5 previously-failing bodied unit tests in `workflowHelpers.test.ts` now pass.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  bfbe8337-ab4e-4d86-a90b-65f8abfcb8ad:
    id: bfbe8337-ab4e-4d86-a90b-65f8abfcb8ad
    content: 'Shipped: sibling-preferred `checkRecurse` in `src/renderer/store/tree/actions/workflowExecutionActions.ts`. When the supplied step has `metadata.decomposition === true`, the new helper picks the next waiting sibling first (independent of the `recurse` flag, since decomposition itself implies sibling sequencing). When no waiting sibling remains the function falls through to today''s chain-traversal path (still gated by `recurse: true`) so this PR can''t regress workflows that rely on cross-chain recurse. Extracted `scheduleRecurseStart` to share the `MAX_RECURSE_ITERATIONS` check, the `recurseCounters` bump, and the 2000ms `setTimeout` between both branches, so the sibling sequence inherits the existing limit + visual rhythm without duplication.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  f81fff8f-94b6-431c-8a79-6c4f2ad92106:
    id: f81fff8f-94b6-431c-8a79-6c4f2ad92106
    content: 'Shipped: multi-root play-forward kick-off in `handleAutonomousFeedback`. Captures `decompositionStepId` (via `getParentIdOrNull(nodeId, ancestorRegistry)`) before `AcceptFeedbackCommand` runs — the multi-root strategy deletes the collaborating node''s ancestry, so the anchor must be read from the pre-accept registry. After `cleanupAutonomousCollaboration` and `advanceOrClearCollaborating` finish, calls `checkRecurse(decompositionStepId, entry.terminalTabId)` to start the first sibling. Subsequent siblings cascade naturally: each sibling''s `completeWorkflow` calls `checkRecurse(position.currentStepId, …)`, which falls through to chain-traversal that walks back to the decomposition step and finds the next waiting sibling via `findNextWaitingNode`.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  c4f82240-b0ea-4336-bb8d-ec0ae00dcdba:
    id: c4f82240-b0ea-4336-bb8d-ec0ae00dcdba
    content: 'AC verification: multi-root path-forward (the new direct kick-off), single-root unchanged (Array.isArray guard), parse-failure unchanged (existing early return), MAX_RECURSE_ITERATIONS now applies across siblings (shared via `scheduleRecurseStart`), UI feedback unchanged (sibling start uses the same `startWorkflow → executeInTerminal → flashNode/toast` chain as a single-node advance).'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
