  ef23a314-089f-4722-a87c-87c6ccf7f77b:
    id: ef23a314-089f-4722-a87c-87c6ccf7f77b
    content: 'Manual/checkpoint pause mid-sequence orphans later siblings — AC says "pause like a non-decomposed handoff", but a non-decomposed handoff stops the workflow. If X pauses on a manual step, no rule says Y must run after X is hand-resumed, so Y silently never starts. Add an explicit rule: resuming a paused sibling re-anchors recurse so the remaining siblings continue.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  7b53a6b9-b9d0-4152-b7ec-67c98a56a5e4:
    id: 7b53a6b9-b9d0-4152-b7ec-67c98a56a5e4
    content: Same-terminal sequencing races with advanceNode — N is advanced to its next step before checkRecurse picks X, so X (decomposition step) and N (next step) compete for the same terminal. Either X must wait until N's pipeline fully completes, or "sequential on the same terminal" needs a sharper definition. This is the highest-risk gap in the spec.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  eb59f400-8558-432d-9b1d-45f49e8951b9:
    id: eb59f400-8558-432d-9b1d-45f49e8951b9
    content: Recurse-without-decomposition warning will fire repeatedly — checkRecurse runs per advance, so a workflow with recurse but no decomposition will toast the warning on every step. Needs a once-per-run guard and ideally a static check at workflow-start time.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  0a5c7832-13fb-4008-8203-9f524356e70c:
    id: 0a5c7832-13fb-4008-8203-9f524356e70c
    content: Existing `.arbo` files that relied on cross-chain recurse silently stop working — the warning toast covers visibility, but user content can be downgraded without the user noticing during a run that previously completed. Worth a one-shot migration notice or a startup-time scan.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  09890dbf-0368-4b32-84ac-28f69ba0cef6:
    id: 09890dbf-0368-4b32-84ac-28f69ba0cef6
    content: completeWorkflow also calls checkRecurse with `position.currentStepId` (line 367) — the new sibling-only lookup must locate the originating decomposition step from any caller, not just from `previousParentId` at advanceNode-time. Anchor-selection is the bulk of the new helper, not traversal.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  6dd572e9-f542-4904-8695-bb8d3235685d:
