  50518ba1-098e-427f-9078-1884e32c2ff3:
    id: 50518ba1-098e-427f-9078-1884e32c2ff3
    content: 'Shipped: chain-traversal fallback removed from `checkRecurse`. The function now tries the supplied step first, walks the surrounding workflow to its decomposition step (via the new `findDecompositionStepInWorkflow` helper) and tries that next, and stops if neither yields a waiting sibling. No more `findFirstAutonomousStepInChain` / `findNextWaitingNode` chain walk — siblings are the only thing recurse processes.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  31b16a13-6d97-4f28-a707-70ed998001c5:
    id: 31b16a13-6d97-4f28-a707-70ed998001c5
    content: 'Shipped: recurse-without-decomposition warning toast + once-per-run guard. When `recurse: true` is set on a step but no step in the surrounding workflow has `decomposition: true`, `checkRecurse` emits the toast `"Warning, you have recursion set without decomposition"` and a paired `notifyWorkflowEvent(''alert'', …)`. A factory-scoped `Set<terminalId>` (`recurseWithoutDecompositionWarned`) gates the toast so it fires once per terminal even after multiple advances.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  30885878-f399-4305-8c4f-1dd6f8b085d6:
    id: 30885878-f399-4305-8c4f-1dd6f8b085d6
    content: 'Shipped: helper text in `StepOptionsSection`. The existing `step-config-description` paragraphs (the light-grey style already used elsewhere in the dialog) now mention the dependency: the decomposition description ends with "Pair with Recurse on a later step to play each sibling forward automatically", and the recurse description reads "After completing this step, automatically process the next decomposed sibling on the same terminal. Requires Decomposition on a step in this workflow — without it, recurse does nothing." No new CSS class needed — the existing style is the spec''d "light grey helper text".'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  7919bc17-7a9e-4e0a-b3c0-8b594fa37a17:
    id: 7919bc17-7a9e-4e0a-b3c0-8b594fa37a17
    content: 'Shipped: `findDecompositionStepInWorkflow(stepId, nodes, ancestorRegistry)` in `workflowHelpers.ts` replaces the deleted `findFirstAutonomousStepInChain`. It walks ancestry to find the nearest enclosing workflow (using `findLast` so nested workflows are scoped correctly) and returns the first child step in that workflow that has `decomposition: true`, or null. Used by checkRecurse for both the sibling-anchor lookup and the "is there any decomposition step?" warning gate, so there''s a single source of truth.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  5e2625d0-7170-4a77-a72b-cfe1c1409035:
    id: 5e2625d0-7170-4a77-a72b-cfe1c1409035
    content: 'Bodied previously-`it.todo` tests now that the implementation is concrete: 2 `chain-traversal removal (PR2)` tests assert that a recurse step in a no-decomposition workflow does not start earlier-step nodes, and that the workflow stops without picking up unrelated chain nodes after the last sibling. 2 `decomposition + recurse dependency helper text (PR2)` tests in `StepConfigDialog.test.tsx` assert the descriptions beneath each checkbox mention the coupled option (case-insensitive regex match so the implementation isn''t over-coupled to the exact wording).'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  bc77a91f-9873-438d-b7c8-ac6621409f11:
    id: bc77a91f-9873-438d-b7c8-ac6621409f11
    content: 'Updated existing tests that relied on cross-chain recurse: the `recurse with completeWorkflow` test now uses `decomposition: true` on the originating step (its assertion that task-b starts after task-a completes still holds via the sibling lookup), and the two safety-limit tests (`recurse safety limit` + `notification wiring`''s recurse-limit case) add `decomposition: true` to step-1 so the iteration goes through the sibling-finder. The previously-failing `workflowHasDecompositionStep walks the nearest enclosing workflow only` test was renamed to `findDecompositionStepInWorkflow walks the nearest enclosing workflow only` and asserts the helper returns null for a deeper-workflow step whose decomposition lives in the outer workflow.'
    children: []
