  0d9dc784-dd35-49c9-a317-9b9caae808c1:
    id: 0d9dc784-dd35-49c9-a317-9b9caae808c1
    content: Context — Arborescent currently funnels every copy through a markdown-tree serializer, so even a single leaf node lands on the system clipboard as `# [ ] Title\n\nBody`. When users copy a node to paste into Slack, email, a browser AI chat, or another node's body, they have to manually strip the heading and checkbox prefix.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  07aca3b1-e1df-4b69-8acb-4fb9f073784a:
    id: 07aca3b1-e1df-4b69-8acb-4fb9f073784a
    content: User — power users who treat individual nodes as text containers and routinely copy a node's content into external apps or another node's body
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  a5e97dcf-2089-409f-ba25-6f11378ed49f:
    id: a5e97dcf-2089-409f-ba25-6f11378ed49f
    content: Current experience — copying a leaf node yields markdown chrome (`# [ ]`, blank line, body); pasting anywhere outside an Arborescent tree exposes the chrome and forces manual cleanup
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  88d51e7f-3eb3-40ef-a27d-b3a9ae31a2cd:
    id: 88d51e7f-3eb3-40ef-a27d-b3a9ae31a2cd
    content: Goal — copying a single leaf node puts only its content on the clipboard so external pastes land clean and internal pastes still round-trip
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  57d78f04-1c3e-4b5d-b50f-cb7a76a18fdb:
    id: 57d78f04-1c3e-4b5d-b50f-cb7a76a18fdb
    content: Business rules
    children:
      - af898d87-3793-4ab6-a4ec-cb0e2dec1084
      - 8fbc6687-3e56-4273-a6b2-886e489c9b68
      - 8e8b7344-96d6-4a83-97d7-e01ae9756591
      - f2112bfa-cc74-4797-952b-42f9bd902529
      - 7c5d4429-a1ba-4ab2-a720-80ef3c5f3ea9
      - 035387f8-8c12-416c-a876-8f94a6fb505d
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  af898d87-3793-4ab6-a4ec-cb0e2dec1084:
    id: af898d87-3793-4ab6-a4ec-cb0e2dec1084
    content: 1. When the selection is a single node with no children, the system clipboard receives only the node's content; if both title and body are present they are joined as `Title\n\nBody`, and an empty half is dropped (no leading blank line, no trailing newline).
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  8fbc6687-3e56-4273-a6b2-886e489c9b68:
    id: 8fbc6687-3e56-4273-a6b2-886e489c9b68
    content: 2. When the selection is a single node that has at least one child, the existing markdown-tree serialization is preserved unchanged, because a parent-with-children is a subtree and has no faithful plain-text rendering.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  8e8b7344-96d6-4a83-97d7-e01ae9756591:
    id: 8e8b7344-96d6-4a83-97d7-e01ae9756591
    content: 3. When the selection contains two or more nodes, the existing markdown-tree serialization is preserved unchanged so structure survives the round trip.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  f2112bfa-cc74-4797-952b-42f9bd902529:
    id: f2112bfa-cc74-4797-952b-42f9bd902529
    content: 4. Cut produces the same clipboard payload as copy.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  7c5d4429-a1ba-4ab2-a720-80ef3c5f3ea9:
    id: 7c5d4429-a1ba-4ab2-a720-80ef3c5f3ea9
    content: 5. Body content is copied verbatim — markdown the user typed inside the body (e.g. their own `# Heading`) is never stripped; only the generated heading and checkbox wrapper is removed.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  035387f8-8c12-416c-a876-8f94a6fb505d:
    id: 035387f8-8c12-416c-a876-8f94a6fb505d
    content: 6. Pasting a freshly copied selection back into Arborescent in the same session reconstructs the original nodes via the in-memory clipboard cache, so internal copy→paste round-trips without re-parsing the clipboard text.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
