      plugins: {}
  79b1baff-f238-458f-96ec-15d553de5e59:
    id: 79b1baff-f238-458f-96ec-15d553de5e59
    content: Cache-miss paste-back is silently lossy — once the clipboardCacheStore entry is evicted or the clipboard is touched by another app, pasting plain content back falls through to `parseMarkdown`, which requires a `#` heading and will produce nothing usable. The markdown-tree path degrades to a parsable tree on cache miss; the plain-content path degrades to "paste does nothing". Decide whether that's acceptable or whether the cache needs a longer lifetime for plain payloads.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: abandoned
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  cb4a0cc0-1a05-4cb6-a485-917272a785bc:
    id: cb4a0cc0-1a05-4cb6-a485-917272a785bc
    content: False cache hits become more likely — the cache keys on exact clipboard string. Plain leaf payloads (e.g. a single short title) collide far more easily with text copied from other apps than today's `# [ ]`-prefixed markdown does, so an external copy that happens to match a cached payload will paste as the cached node. Worth a guard (e.g. clear cache on focus loss, or fingerprint with a zero-width marker).
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: abandoned
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  98fae602-5d1c-42e8-ad22-0db009e4d274:
    id: 98fae602-5d1c-42e8-ad22-0db009e4d274
    content: AC gap on the empty leaf — behavior when both title and body are empty isn't specified (empty-string clipboard write vs. no-op vs. fall through to markdown). Pick one and add an AC.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: abandoned
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  f911b6a0-727c-4b17-99a6-6eb8ff7cd2ff:
    id: f911b6a0-727c-4b17-99a6-6eb8ff7cd2ff
    content: 'AC #5 vs. round-trip on cache miss — a body that begins with `# [ ]` is copied verbatim (correct per rule 5), but on cache-miss paste-back `parseMarkdown` will interpret it as a heading. Round-trip is only guaranteed via the in-memory cache, which is worth stating explicitly so reviewers don''t read AC #8 as a stronger guarantee than it is.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: abandoned
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
