    content: 'Body-only edge case left as `it.todo` — AC 3 ("Copying a single leaf node with only a body puts just the body on the clipboard") cannot be expressed unambiguously against the data model: `TreeNode.content` is a single string field, with no separate title/body. The "body-only" shape (e.g. `\n\nBar`) requires a normalisation decision (verbatim vs. trim leading newlines) that AC 5 ("verbatim") and AC 3 don''t reconcile. Marked as title-only `it.todo` per the "post-fix behavior is uncertain" guidance.'
