  478b3a96-67b1-4250-9d65-2193a089dd25:
    id: 478b3a96-67b1-4250-9d65-2193a089dd25
    content: Legacy contexts saved before the boolean refactor have `execute` and `collaborate` as `undefined`. `useAppliedContexts.ts` already compensates by treating "both undefined" as `collaborate=true, execute=false`. The new partition must apply the same fallback before bucketing, otherwise every pre-refactor context declaration silently lands in `Actions` and disappears from where users currently find it.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: abandoned
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  8c2ca106-0073-4ed6-978d-393ef74bff41:
    id: 8c2ca106-0073-4ed6-978d-393ef74bff41
    content: The submenu's all-sections-empty case must still return `null` after the four-way partition — the existing early-out only checks `availableContexts.length === 0 && !showBuiltIns`, which still holds, but the assembly loop must not emit a stray leading separator or `Close`-only menu when every section is empty under `showBuiltIns=true`.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  dc2214df-09aa-42b0-bc2f-58b1293b818a:
    id: dc2214df-09aa-42b0-bc2f-58b1293b818a
    content: Header ordering inconsistency (`Execute & Collaborate` in the menu vs `Collaborate & Execute` in tooltips/labels via `flagsLabel`) is user-visible if the same context is shown in both surfaces; flagged but kept out of scope per the spec — worth a follow-up only if QA confirms it is jarring.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: abandoned
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  63453fff-679a-4d5c-bb60-f75f424d01ea:
    id: 63453fff-679a-4d5c-bb60-f75f424d01ea
    content: 'ROI is comfortably positive: the change is a single-file partition swap plus tests, and it unblocks the `Actions` flag combination which is currently unreachable via the menu.'
    children: []
