  6226d5b7-be9a-4865-b38b-ec012103a61b:
    id: 6226d5b7-be9a-4865-b38b-ec012103a61b
    content: Replace the two-filter grouping in `useSetContextSubmenu.ts` with a single pass that buckets each context by its normalised `(execute, collaborate)` tuple — applying the same legacy `undefined → collaborate=true` default used by `useAppliedContexts.ts` so historical files keep working.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  131a960d-72a4-4c5e-b886-058bb2747fd3:
    id: 131a960d-72a4-4c5e-b886-058bb2747fd3
    content: Drive menu assembly from an ordered `[Actions, Execute, Collaborate, Execute & Collaborate]` section list, emitting a header + items only when the bucket (or its built-in) is non-empty, and inserting separators only between consecutively-rendered sections.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  2ef7daeb-b5a8-407f-9586-bdc4b0ed2291:
    id: 2ef7daeb-b5a8-407f-9586-bdc4b0ed2291
    content: Built-in `Basic execution` / `Basic review` stay inside the `Execute` / `Collaborate` sections respectively, so the `showBuiltIns` gate and existing radio/inheritance behaviour are untouched.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  33631fc5-67b4-4903-a229-41fd7800748d:
    id: 33631fc5-67b4-4903-a229-41fd7800748d
    content: Legacy `undefined`-flag contexts are not normalised inside `useSetContextSubmenu` because `ContextDeclarationInfo` is already strictly-typed `boolean` (coerced upstream via `=== true` in `buildContextDeclarations`). Pre-refactor contexts with both flags missing therefore land in `Actions` rather than `Collaborate`. Out of scope for this PR — fixing it requires changing `buildContextDeclarations` (a different file/touchpoint), and per spec we did not expand scope.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: abandoned
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
