  b0d73fc3-5f20-4efc-9270-1e58e1249366:
    id: b0d73fc3-5f20-4efc-9270-1e58e1249366
    content: 'Recurse semantics — clarified: recurse is conditionally terminal, not unconditionally terminal. When a node passes through a recurse step:'
    children:
      - 77f04ec1-5f5f-4cdb-a011-1ec70163521d
      - d3bf6896-a763-4d38-9d04-4466297e6d55
      - 2cbd92dd-24b4-4ba4-917c-695103ffafe6
      - b005e024-7bd0-4345-969c-81d0c5c01007
      - 905242f5-c2f4-492b-8de6-f5db21acdb32
      - b9b70d3a-62ad-4b97-8ce8-01ea90dafc57
      - e7baa403-ab86-4d6e-a187-f2969a3769fc
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  77f04ec1-5f5f-4cdb-a011-1ec70163521d:
    id: 77f04ec1-5f5f-4cdb-a011-1ec70163521d
    content: If no related decomposed nodes are found, the node continues to the next step (recurse is transparent in the no-fan-out case).
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  d3bf6896-a763-4d38-9d04-4466297e6d55:
    id: d3bf6896-a763-4d38-9d04-4466297e6d55
    content: If related decomposed nodes are found, this node stops at recurse so the related nodes can be processed.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  2cbd92dd-24b4-4ba4-917c-695103ffafe6:
    id: 2cbd92dd-24b4-4ba4-917c-695103ffafe6
    content: When several related nodes each finish their chain through recurse, every one of them stops — including the last. There is no automatic fan-in to a post-recurse step; the user must decide how to reintegrate the parallel outcomes.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  b005e024-7bd0-4345-969c-81d0c5c01007:
    id: b005e024-7bd0-4345-969c-81d0c5c01007
    content: 'Rationale: a post-recurse step typically represents a reintegration task (e.g. work to do after all PRs in a user story are done). Auto-advancing the last sibling would skip the decision the user is supposed to make about how to combine the parallel outcomes.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  905242f5-c2f4-492b-8de6-f5db21acdb32:
    id: 905242f5-c2f4-492b-8de6-f5db21acdb32
    content: 'To clarify, Last step means :'
    children:
      - 98af54fc-db89-4ee9-bb69-20bc5a9eea18
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  98af54fc-db89-4ee9-bb69-20bc5a9eea18:
    id: 98af54fc-db89-4ee9-bb69-20bc5a9eea18
    content: Last autonomous or checkpoint step in a chain - there is either no next step, or the next step is manual.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  b9b70d3a-62ad-4b97-8ce8-01ea90dafc57:
    id: b9b70d3a-62ad-4b97-8ce8-01ea90dafc57
    content: 'Implication for "last step" detection: a recurse step that found related siblings is effectively a last step for the executing node, even if a non-manual successor is configured. Completion detection must recognize this conditional-terminal case alongside the literal-no-next-step case.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  e7baa403-ab86-4d6e-a187-f2969a3769fc:
    id: e7baa403-ab86-4d6e-a187-f2969a3769fc
    content: No validation guard is required — users can place any step type after a recurse step; the runtime decides at execution time whether to advance or stop based on whether related decomposed nodes were found.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  4c119769-c420-4f37-b44a-cc56ce1935e3:
    id: 4c119769-c420-4f37-b44a-cc56ce1935e3
    content: Symptom vs. state — the green arrow is the indicator; the underlying bug could be (a) the in-memory store still says running, (b) the persisted running flag on the workflow root never got cleared, or (c) the store is correct but the indicator selector reads a stale field. Need to check all three before patching only the visible end.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  0e0c5784-c2f2-4b36-9ad3-29d3bb51ebc6:
    id: 0e0c5784-c2f2-4b36-9ad3-29d3bb51ebc6
    content: Persistence and restart — if the running flag is persisted, existing `.arbo` files in the field may already have stuck-running workflows. Decide whether the fix only repairs new completions or also self-heals on load (e.g. if no terminal/process is associated with the workflow on startup, clear the flag rather than treating the workflow as resumable).
    children:
      - a2aaa3bf-9086-4101-8537-7edd29bf79be
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  a2aaa3bf-9086-4101-8537-7edd29bf79be:
    id: a2aaa3bf-9086-4101-8537-7edd29bf79be
    content: No don't worry about that I'll cleanup manually, I'm the only person using the workflow feature for now
    children: []
