  9b1d7acc-cde2-4704-a364-4210f0963f0d:
    id: 9b1d7acc-cde2-4704-a364-4210f0963f0d
    content: Land the fix on the workflow-completion path in `workflowExecutionActions` (and the recurse driver). When a chain ends — final numbered step finished, node stopped at recurse-with-related-siblings, recurse iterator's sibling queue drained, or 50-iteration cap hit — call the same teardown that the disruption paths (terminal close, item delete/move, app restart) already use, so completion converges on `stopWorkflow`/clear-running rather than its own bespoke path.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  ff7d8312-2dc8-4d41-9350-03da7c2c3d74:
    id: ff7d8312-2dc8-4d41-9350-03da7c2c3d74
    content: 'Workflow-idle is multi-chain under decomposition + recurse: each spawned sibling is its own chain that ends at the recurse step. The workflow only goes idle once every spawned chain has ended and no further sibling is queued. A post-recurse step waiting for manual reintegration must NOT keep the workflow flagged as running — the arrow goes off, the user takes over.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  9bb9947c-dba3-4fcf-bdcf-3581564a09f1:
    id: 9bb9947c-dba3-4fcf-bdcf-3581564a09f1
    content: 'Pin the fix with one regression test per completion shape that exists today: linear final-step completion, recurse-pass-through (no related siblings; node advances past recurse normally), decomposition+recurse last-sibling stop with a non-manual successor present (workflow goes idle, post-recurse step is left for manual reintegration), recurse-cap stop, and (if intermittent) one targeted test for whichever path the repro identifies. The disruption-handling tests already prove the teardown works; this test set proves completion calls it.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  5b89103c-4a21-4ae1-8bd3-249fe1055c98:
    id: 5b89103c-4a21-4ae1-8bd3-249fe1055c98
    content: Non-obvious for a reviewer — the visible green arrow is downstream of the workflow's running flag, so the right diff is one or two lines on the completion side, not in the indicator component. Also, the keep-awake block release is gated on the running flag being cleared, so this fix likely also stops the system being held awake after the workflow really finished — worth verifying as a side effect.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
