  72bac13e-7ee6-456a-b6d8-84d1173dbf55:
    id: 72bac13e-7ee6-456a-b6d8-84d1173dbf55
    content: Context — Today, an AI session lives inside whichever terminal tab the user invoked it in. When a long autonomous step is running, that tab is effectively pinned to it; if the user closes the tab they lose the session, and if they walk away mid-step there is no UI to come back to it. To run several workflow steps in parallel without babysitting, the user wants the workflow to spin sessions up and tear them down on its own, and to be able to reattach to any active step from a fresh terminal tab.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  4d21cc74-7fdd-46cb-bf8a-86b93ca38a15:
    id: 4d21cc74-7fdd-46cb-bf8a-86b93ca38a15
    content: User — anyone running workflow steps that invoke a terminal AI session, particularly those running multiple in parallel or stepping away mid-step.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  9c0215d1-ed08-46ed-8c7f-b49a0d971980:
    id: 9c0215d1-ed08-46ed-8c7f-b49a0d971980
    content: Current experience — sessions are coupled 1:1 to the visible terminal tab. Closing the tab kills the session; switching tabs leaves it running but unfindable; resuming requires manually constructing a CLI flag in the right working directory. No node-level affordance to reopen a step that was started earlier.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  84246b0d-ea4b-498a-8d27-c5db50f487be:
    id: 84246b0d-ea4b-498a-8d27-c5db50f487be
    content: Goal — every workflow step that opens an AI session captures the session identifier on its node and offers a one-click "Resume session" from any terminal tab, surviving app restart. Starting a workflow auto-spawns a fresh terminal + session (or attaches to/resumes the workflow's prior session if one is still alive), and `recurse` chains stay inside the same session as the node they recursed from.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  cc66497e-eefa-44f1-8e97-a9c059e6ea7d:
    id: cc66497e-eefa-44f1-8e97-a9c059e6ea7d
    content: Key distinction — "workflow stopped" and "session ended" are independent states. A workflow can be stopped from Arborescent's side while its underlying CLI session is still running in an open terminal tab. The feature must reason about *session liveness* (process + tab state), not workflow status, when deciding spawn vs resume vs attach.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  12946fa7-a8a4-4fa1-948c-973ee9ea6b5a:
    id: 12946fa7-a8a4-4fa1-948c-973ee9ea6b5a
    content: Business rules covered here — 7 (default new-terminal spawn), 8 (three-tier priority on start), 9 (no duplicate tab for same session id).
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
