    content: '- [ ] A node reached via `recurse` whose parent session is alive and attached to an open tab sends its prompt to that tab and does not open a new one.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  1bb1d7b6-86cd-4f14-ad8d-e17a8e22abec:
    id: 1bb1d7b6-86cd-4f14-ad8d-e17a8e22abec
    content: '- [ ] A node reached via `recurse` whose parent session is alive but whose tab is closed opens a new tab, resumes the parent''s session there, and sends its prompt to it. The recursed node records the inherited session id.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  e94659b0-4549-4af6-9f2b-922789af7b97:
    id: e94659b0-4549-4af6-9f2b-922789af7b97
    content: '- [ ] A node reached via `recurse` whose parent session is dead spawns a fresh session, surfaces the broken-chain state, and is recorded with the new session id.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  be1b3ba4-7a47-4256-afa9-529d8a33c8e7:
    id: be1b3ba4-7a47-4256-afa9-529d8a33c8e7
    content: '- [ ] When a session is hosted by a tab that gets closed and later resumed in a new tab, every node bound to that session (including recurse descendants) refreshes its terminal pointer; no node sends prompts to the closed tab.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  2a197fb9-591e-4c03-9bdf-ea88906f0ef0:
