  503ef390-d883-4914-b665-c3d140cd978f:
    id: 503ef390-d883-4914-b665-c3d140cd978f
    content: Context — Terminal-based AI sessions (collaborations and workflow steps) bind a node to a terminal. Users running multiple parallel sessions lose track of which node a focused terminal is currently driving; the only existing cues are the prompt header and inferring from output.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  b105ff95-bd15-41f6-9bc3-14561822a1a4:
    id: b105ff95-bd15-41f6-9bc3-14561822a1a4
    content: User — Anyone running multiple terminal-based AI sessions in parallel
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  268cd003-933a-4efc-9370-eebd62343aa5:
    id: 268cd003-933a-4efc-9370-eebd62343aa5
    content: Current experience and gap — Switching terminals gives no visual feedback in the tree about the active session's target node. Users mentally re-anchor on each switch, which is error-prone during long autonomous runs.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  b3d50c05-91dc-4791-aefb-95fc05ac76a8:
    id: b3d50c05-91dc-4791-aefb-95fc05ac76a8
    content: Goal — Focusing a terminal visually highlights the node it is currently driving so the user can see the binding at a glance.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
