      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  54465ba7-894f-4245-be88-4ab9cd2aa8d5:
    id: 54465ba7-894f-4245-be88-4ab9cd2aa8d5
    content: Focused-terminal id may not exist as Zustand state today — terminal focus may currently live only in DOM/xterm. If so, the story implicitly adds a small piece of persisted state plus a focus-event listener; cost is low but it is a real touchpoint, not a no-op selector.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  9c0a3b06-d14b-470c-b468-8f19c2435ded:
    id: 9c0a3b06-d14b-470c-b468-8f19c2435ded
    content: 'Workflow steps can nest — when a parent workflow drives a child sub-workflow on the same terminal, the "bound node" is ambiguous. Decision needed: highlight the deepest running step only, or also highlight ancestors. Default to leaf-only to keep the visual signal sharp.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: abandoned
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  e1b64122-f85e-46eb-a27c-d73eb3a3e6dd:
    id: e1b64122-f85e-46eb-a27c-d73eb3a3e6dd
    content: 'A single terminal can host a workflow step AND have a free-form collaboration started on a different node concurrently. Decision needed: workflow takes precedence, or last-bound wins. Default to workflow-step-wins because workflow execution is the reason terminals get focused programmatically.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  203834c5-5ed3-4605-a46d-9b3d8cfb84cc:
    id: 203834c5-5ed3-4605-a46d-9b3d8cfb84cc
    content: The "only two nodes re-render" AC is real work, not free — TreeNode must subscribe with `state => state.activeSessionNodeId === ownId` (boolean), not to the raw id. Subscribing to the raw id will re-render every TreeNode on every focus switch.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  9d1dadfd-0eb4-453c-8e19-051019f6818a:
    id: 9d1dadfd-0eb4-453c-8e19-051019f6818a
    content: 'Out of scope, intentional: scroll-into-view, breadcrumb header in the tree, reciprocal highlight (clicking a node does not focus its terminal), and any change to terminal-tab styling.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  294d1dfd-8920-4d42-bb40-ac9d0e78e0c4:
    id: 294d1dfd-8920-4d42-bb40-ac9d0e78e0c4
    content: Summarise the approach
    children:
      - 6c849dfd-68d3-4272-90c2-a31ca60ae245
      - 5dda83a0-2ae7-4e22-b901-42eab3146191
      - 996d410a-2fc0-4f45-81eb-f8310a37b361
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  6c849dfd-68d3-4272-90c2-a31ca60ae245:
    id: 6c849dfd-68d3-4272-90c2-a31ca60ae245
    content: 'Architecture: one new derived selector in the tree store fed by three existing inputs (focused-terminal id, collaboratingNodeId, workflow session map). No new IPC, no new persisted state on disk, no new commands.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  5dda83a0-2ae7-4e22-b901-42eab3146191:
    id: 5dda83a0-2ae7-4e22-b901-42eab3146191
    content: 'Where it lands: tree store selector, TreeNode component (boolean prop subscription + class toggle), globals.css for the highlight rule. Touches the terminal store only if focused-terminal id is not already there.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  996d410a-2fc0-4f45-81eb-f8310a37b361:
    id: 996d410a-2fc0-4f45-81eb-f8310a37b361
    content: 'Non-obvious: TreeNode subscription shape (`isActiveSession: boolean` selector per node) is what makes the AC about "only two nodes re-render" hold; reviewers should look there first.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  61c341e7-a0c1-4a7e-b5cc-19e98f31bea6:
    id: 61c341e7-a0c1-4a7e-b5cc-19e98f31bea6
    content: Decomposition not warranted — one selector + one CSS rule + one TreeNode class toggle (plus optional focused-terminal-id wiring); splitting any of these into separate PRs would land dead plumbing in master with no user value, violating "Each chunk must be a coherent piece of the feature"
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  cf2e2bff-bc1b-4696-bfe8-8985d08a1571:
    id: cf2e2bff-bc1b-4696-bfe8-8985d08a1571
    content: Nested-workflow leaf-vs-ancestor precedence not strictly enforced — selector returns the first running step found via Object.entries iteration, which is unstable across runtimes; unit test currently accepts either nodeId. Defer until real nested-workflow usage shows whether leaf-only is actually preferred.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: abandoned
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
