  d30accac-717d-4088-bd5b-b6845d7887ab:
    id: d30accac-717d-4088-bd5b-b6845d7887ab
    content: Context — Arborescent nodes already hold commands and snippets users keep alongside notes; today they have to be copied out and reformatted by hand before they run, so the markdown syntax leaks into the terminal.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  e23e3fa8-de36-46b2-8949-af83355afe0c:
    id: e23e3fa8-de36-46b2-8949-af83355afe0c
    content: User — Developer using Arborescent to keep runnable commands organised next to documentation
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  c8560157-3b3e-46de-bec8-aada89384b87:
    id: c8560157-3b3e-46de-bec8-aada89384b87
    content: Current experience — Sending a node passes its markdown verbatim, so backticks, list bullets, and other syntax characters reach the terminal as literal text and the command fails or runs incorrectly
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  653f8071-0d57-476b-88ed-28018607a379:
    id: 653f8071-0d57-476b-88ed-28018607a379
    content: Goal — Let a user execute a single selected node against the terminal when the node is unambiguously a command, while keeping the same nodes available as prose when the intent is review, editing, or sharing
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  04ee8084-9095-473b-a338-3b6be11b834e:
    id: 04ee8084-9095-473b-a338-3b6be11b834e
    content: Business rules
    children:
      - fbac0970-1d02-450a-94fb-01a2235459ad
      - 2a9c8e68-9374-4b43-b8ae-bd02953fff1f
      - f1889bdf-0c30-4dcc-9103-c5bd9a8bf0e0
      - d3285711-99ec-4d50-bc4c-ad3d73a4e459
      - 91101070-fec1-42c9-9914-9c13baf72b8c
      - da1c711e-6caf-4b55-b51f-1690164dfd7c
      - 55e73592-dadd-4b4e-b255-1bf8fc552911
      - e91494af-f38c-44bb-8893-2b7125f0e425
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  fbac0970-1d02-450a-94fb-01a2235459ad:
    id: fbac0970-1d02-450a-94fb-01a2235459ad
    content: 1. A node is a code-node candidate only when its entire content is wrapped in backticks; a node that mixes a backticked span with any other text or block is a normal node.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  2a9c8e68-9374-4b43-b8ae-bd02953fff1f:
    id: 2a9c8e68-9374-4b43-b8ae-bd02953fff1f
    content: 2. A code-node candidate is demoted to a normal node if it has children or has any context applied, since either signals review/editing intent rather than execution intent.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  f1889bdf-0c30-4dcc-9103-c5bd9a8bf0e0:
    id: f1889bdf-0c30-4dcc-9103-c5bd9a8bf0e0
    content: 3. Execution as a command happens only when the selection is exactly one code node; any selection of two or more nodes is sent as markdown, even if every selected node would individually pass the code test.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  d3285711-99ec-4d50-bc4c-ad3d73a4e459:
    id: d3285711-99ec-4d50-bc4c-ad3d73a4e459
    content: 4. A single-code-node send reaches the terminal as raw text with the wrapping backticks stripped and is dispatched as one command.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  91101070-fec1-42c9-9914-9c13baf72b8c:
    id: 91101070-fec1-42c9-9914-9c13baf72b8c
    content: 5. Normal-node sends are emitted as markdown to the destination and are not executed as shell commands.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  da1c711e-6caf-4b55-b51f-1690164dfd7c:
    id: da1c711e-6caf-4b55-b51f-1690164dfd7c
    content: 6. Backticked spans inside any markdown-rendered output display as codeblocks, matching the behaviour seen in Slack, GitLab, and GitHub comment panels.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  55e73592-dadd-4b4e-b255-1bf8fc552911:
    id: 55e73592-dadd-4b4e-b255-1bf8fc552911
    content: 7. An empty or whitespace-only node sends nothing instead of dispatching a blank command.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  e91494af-f38c-44bb-8893-2b7125f0e425:
    id: e91494af-f38c-44bb-8893-2b7125f0e425
    content: 8. If no terminal is connected when a single-code-node send is attempted, the action surfaces a user-visible error rather than failing silently.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: pending
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  f7f31f51-6288-4853-8969-2e270523b506:
