  287e4f73-d942-454b-bb27-761e1f4b5f2e:
    id: 287e4f73-d942-454b-bb27-761e1f4b5f2e
    content: Routing fix landed in src/renderer/hooks/useHookEventListener.ts — SessionStart routes via terminal_id (using useTerminalStore.fileStates ownership); Stop/NeedsReview/Notification/UserPromptSubmit/unknown route via session_id (workflowSessionMap lookup); orphan events dropped with warn log; lifecycle (mount/unmount) preserved. All 21 routing tests pass; original useHookEventListener.test.ts (9 tests, harness updated to provide ownership/session-map fakes) still passes; eslint clean on changed files; tsc --noEmit clean.
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  5e8fe32f-aa1b-4022-90f3-c21780a18cdb:
    id: 5e8fe32f-aa1b-4022-90f3-c21780a18cdb
    content: 'Verification: traced each User-story symptom to its mechanism in src/renderer/store/tree/actions/workflowExecutionActions.ts — `registerSession` (line 525) mutates `workflowSessionMap` and evicts prior session→terminal mappings (root cause of "now assigned to another") and, on source=''clear'', invokes `clearSessionManager.onClearConfirmed` for the running node on `terminalId` (root cause of duplicate commands when broadcast); `handleHookEvent` Stop path mutates `workflowExecutionStates` (root cause of cross-store false-positive "already assigned" since `findRunningNodeOnTerminal` reads it). Routing at the dispatch boundary in useHookEventListener.ts is the single chokepoint that prevents all three. Routing tests in tests/useHookEventListenerRouting.test.ts cover all three scenarios cross-cutting (multi-store harness): "does not register a clear-session prompt twice when both stores are open" (duplicate commands), "a SessionStart on file-A''s terminal does not corrupt file-B''s session map" (assigned-to-another), and the routing-only delivery tests for Stop/NeedsReview/Notification/UserPromptSubmit (false-positive elimination). 30/30 useHookEventListener tests pass; 2 pre-existing failures in src/renderer/store/tree/actions/tests/clearAiSessionHookHandler.test.ts ("window.electron.startKeepAwake is not a function") reproduce identically on master and are out of scope for this PR.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  4d4ae726-91fb-4702-a9a1-45edc1fa28c2:
    id: 4d4ae726-91fb-4702-a9a1-45edc1fa28c2
    content: 'Review feedback (pr-review-toolkit:code-reviewer): Bottom line — fix is correct for all three named symptoms; SessionStart→Stop "race" is a non-issue because Zustand set is synchronous and Electron IPC delivers events serially to a single listener. Action items: (1) IMPORTANT — useHookEventListener.ts:11 inside findStoreOwningTerminal does a redundant `getAllStoreEntries().find(...)` after Object.entries already yielded `filePath`; replace with `storeManager.getStoreForFile(filePath)` — functionally equivalent, eliminates a potential silent miss if entry ordering ever drifts. (2) IMPORTANT — add a test for the close-and-reopen scenario: file-A registers session → file-A closes (terminal goes) → Stop arrives for that session → assert no store touched and no false-positive warning on bystander file-B. This is a residual gap the new routing surfaces (the old broadcast tolerated it by accident; new routing silently drops with warn — correct, but uncovered). (3) IMPORTANT — add a terminal_id-collision test: when two files share a terminal_id, `findStoreOwningTerminal` returns first Object.entries match (order-dependent). Either pin "first match wins" explicitly or add an invariant assertion; today probably impossible but the routing layer doesn''t enforce it. (4) MINOR — handleHookEvent in workflowHookEventHandler.ts:63-71 still has its own session-map fallback warn; that''s defense-in-depth but produces a duplicate "dropped" log when reached. Consider distinguishing the listener-side warn ("no store owns session X") from the handler-side warn so logs aren''t ambiguous. (5) MINOR — `findStoreOwningSession` is O(F) per non-SessionStart event (Stop fires every AI turn). Fine today; if file count grows, maintain a reverse `sessionId→store` index in storeManager. (6) MINOR — `storeManager.getAllStoreEntries` is now used by routing; add a one-line intent comment so it doesn''t accidentally become the new broadcast primitive (existing broadcasters still call `getAllStores()` from useTerminalPanel.ts:17, useFeedbackClipboard.ts:107, useAppInitialization.ts:26, uiService.ts:81 — all correct for their concerns). No correctness blockers; ship after (1)+(2)+(3).'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  b8381149-6965-4caa-9eff-2cf31a88b761:
    id: b8381149-6965-4caa-9eff-2cf31a88b761
    content: 'Feedback on the review (developer reply, after reading the actual code): ACCEPTED 1 of 6 findings; REJECTED the rest with reasons. — REJECT (incorrect) Finding 1 "replace getAllStoreEntries().find(...) with getStoreForFile(filePath)": getStoreForFile() is NOT a pure lookup — it AUTO-CREATES a store on miss (storeManager.ts:27-31: `if (!this.stores.has(actualPath)) { ... this.stores.set(actualPath, store); ... }`). Using it from the routing path would spuriously instantiate stores for closed files when late hook events arrive, leaking memory and causing the very cross-store contamination this PR is fixing. The current `getAllStoreEntries().find(...)` is read-only and correct. Severity exaggerated (marked IMPORTANT) — should not have been flagged. ACCEPT Finding 2 "close-and-reopen test": valid coverage gap. Will add a test where file-A registers session, file-A closes (closeFile() at storeManager.ts:59-84 destroys the store + terminals), then a Stop arrives for that session — assert no store mutated, listener warns and drops. REJECT (low probability + intentional) Finding 3 "terminal_id collision test": terminal IDs are generated as `terminal-${Date.now()}` in terminalService.ts:10 from a single renderer process; collisions require two creates in the same millisecond in the same process, which user-driven flow does not produce. Object.entries iteration is spec-deterministic (insertion order); "first-match-wins" is the natural and stable behavior, not an order-drift risk. Adding this test pins implementation detail without protecting against any real bug. Severity exaggerated; intentional behavior presented as issue. REJECT (non-issue) Finding 4 "duplicate dropped log": traced both warn paths — the listener''s `findStoreOwningSession` and the handler''s `if (!terminalId)` (workflowHookEventHandler.ts:64-71) both read `workflowSessionMap` for the SAME store. If the listener finds a store, the handler will too — the handler-side branch is unreachable via the listener path. It''s only reachable on direct test invocation. No actual duplicate log occurs in production. SKIP (acknowledged speculative) Finding 5 "O(F) hot path": reviewer themselves frames as "fine today, future-only". Premature optimization. REJECT (violates project convention) Finding 6 "intent comment on getAllStoreEntries": CLAUDE.md "Code Style"/"Comments" sections explicitly say "Comments for ''why'' not ''what''" and "If code needs a comment explaining what it does, refactor to a named function". A "use this for routing, not broadcasting" comment is a usage/what comment, not a why. If the concern is real, the right move is renaming (e.g., `getEntriesForRouting`) — but with only one routing caller today, that''s premature too. SKIP. NET PLAN: implement Finding 2 only (one new test in tests/useHookEventListenerRouting.test.ts).'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  e6fa6f03-a359-481a-8cfc-22f10ec9ae12:
    id: e6fa6f03-a359-481a-8cfc-22f10ec9ae12
    content: 'Feedback summary by severity — HIGH: none; MEDIUM (accept): Finding 2 (close-and-reopen test); LOW/REJECTED (incorrect): Finding 1 (storeManager auto-creates stores, would regress the fix); LOW/REJECTED (low probability + intentional): Finding 3 (collision impossible with current ID scheme; insertion-order iteration is intentional); LOW/REJECTED (non-issue): Finding 4 (handler-side warn unreachable via listener); LOW/SKIP (speculative): Finding 5 (acknowledged future-only); LOW/REJECTED (violates conventions): Finding 6 (what-comment).'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
  dfe7a415-e672-4ace-8c48-e4836cf6e4f0:
    id: dfe7a415-e672-4ace-8c48-e4836cf6e4f0
    content: 'Documentation decision — no changes needed. Changelog: "Workflow execution" is in CHANGELOG.md ## Unreleased (line 11) and last release tag is v0.1.1 (only `chore` commits since), so this fix targets an unreleased feature → per convention "Don''t add a line to the changelog for a bug fix to a feature that was implemented after the last release", skip. Docs: behavior change is "running workflows in multiple open .arbo files no longer cross-contaminate" — that''s the natural expectation, not a discoverability/usability issue; existing docs/workflows.md:120-122 already cover same-file multi-terminal workflows; cross-file is implicit and non-blocking. Per convention "If it''s implicit or discoverable and non-blocking, no need to mention it" and "Don''t add an entry if it''s not useful to the user or bloats the documentation", skip. No existing docs reference the broken behavior, so nothing to retract.'
    children: []
    metadata:
      status: completed
      expanded: true
      deleted: false
      plugins: {}
